/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"par":{"close":{"tw":[["closure",4],["end",2],["finish",2],["last",0],["complete",2],["draw",3],["plug",3],["open",1]],"en":"Last winter the town decided on the closure of the small library. Nobody wanted to see it close, but the money had run out. My neighbours signed a paper to ask for a new end date. After months of work we managed to complete the repairs ourselves and finish the roof before the cold came. On the last evening a reporter came to draw a picture of the empty hall. We pulled the plug of the old coffee machine and opened every window to let the dust out. It felt like an open door again.","zh":"去年冬天镇上决定关闭那间小图书馆。没有人想看着它关门，但经费已经用完了。邻居们签了一份请愿书，要求给一个新的截止日期。忙了几个月，我们自己修好了屋顶，赶在寒潮前把工程做完。最后一个晚上，一位记者来画下了空荡荡的大厅。我们拔掉了旧咖啡机的插头，把每扇窗都打开放灰尘出去。它又像一扇开着的门了。"},"climb":{"tw":[["steep",6],["raise",0],["move",2],["grow",2],["jump",3],["ride",3],["rise",2],["peak",6],["mount",0]],"en":"The path to the top is steep, and the last hour of it is a slow climb. We begin early, before the sun can raise the heat of the day. Step by step we move up and watch the farms below grow small. My brother likes to jump from rock to rock, while I prefer to ride the old cable car. Every spring more visitors rise with the first light, so we chose a quiet Tuesday instead. At the peak we mount a small flag on the stone and eat our bread in the wind.","zh":"上山顶的路很陡，最后一段更是一步一步地爬。我们很早就出发，趁太阳还没把热气升起来。一级一级往上走，看着下面的农庄变得越来越小。弟弟喜欢在石头间跳来跳去，我更愿意坐那趟旧缆车。每年春天都有更多游客跟着第一缕光上山，所以我们挑了安静的周二。到了山顶，我们在石头上竖了一面小旗，在风里啃面包。"},"shout":{"tw":[["loud",6],["call",0],["scream",3],["cry",0],["curse",3],["noise",3],["express",2],["whisper",1],["talk",2]],"en":"At the school sports day everybody shouts. My father can shout so loud that his voice carries across the whole field. He will call my name and I run faster. When our team scores, the crowd begins to scream and cry with joy. A few boys curse the referee and make a lot of noise, so a teacher tells them to express their feelings in a better way. My quiet aunt does not shout at all; she can only whisper, yet we still talk for hours. Loud or soft, her words reach me.","zh":"学校运动会那天人人都在喊。我爸喊起来响得能穿过整个操场。他一叫我的名字，我就跑得更快。我们队得分时，全场又尖叫又欢呼。有几个男孩骂裁判、闹得很吵，老师让他们换个方式表达情绪。我那位安静的姑妈从来不喊，她只能小声说话，可我们仍能聊上几个小时。无论是喊出来的还是轻声说的，她的话我都能听见。"},"hide":{"tw":[["cover",3],["change",2],["skin",0],["conceal",0],["find",6],["harbor",3],["earth",3],["reveal",6]],"en":"The little fox knows how to hide. It will cover its body with dry leaves and change the colour of its coat with the seasons. In the cold months its skin turns white, which is the best way to conceal itself on snow. We could not find it for a whole week. One morning, near the harbor, it sat on the black earth beside a boat and looked at us. It had been sleeping under that same boat the whole time. Then it moved, and the light seemed to reveal a thin line of red fur along its back.","zh":"那只小狐狸很会藏。它用干叶子盖住身子，还随季节变换毛色。天冷的那几个月，它的皮毛转成白色，这是雪地里最好的隐藏办法。整整一周我们都没找到它。有天早上，在港口附近，它坐在一条船边的黑土上看着我们。接着它一动，光似乎把背脊上一道细细的红毛露了出来。"},"pull":{"tw":[["draw",3],["push",1],["force",2],["tear",0],["move",6],["bring",3],["drive",2],["catch",3]],"en":"Our old car stopped in the mud after the rain. My brother had to pull the small trailer by hand. He used a rope to draw it forward while I pushed from behind with all my force. The work was slow and I began to tear my jacket on the door. A farmer came over to help, and together we managed to move the trailer to the road. He offered to bring his truck and used his tractor to drive both cars home. We did not want to catch a cold in the rain.","zh":"雨后我们那辆旧车陷在泥里。弟弟只好用手拖那个小挂车。他用绳子往前拉，我在后面使劲推。活儿很慢，我的外套在车门上开始撕开了。一位农夫过来帮忙，我俩一起把挂车挪到了路上。他提出开他的卡车来，最后用拖拉机把两辆车都拖回了家。我们可不想在雨里感上风寒。"},"join":{"tw":[["unite",0],["connect",2],["junction",4],["joiner",4],["fair",3],["close",3],["union",0],["meet",6]],"en":"Two villages decided to join their small schools. The teachers wanted to unite the classes and connect the old halls with a new path. At the junction of the two roads the workers built a wide gate, and a joiner made the wooden doors by hand. The two head teachers meet every Monday to plan the week. On the day of the fair, families from both sides came close to the stage and watched the children sing. The union of two schools was not easy, but now nobody can tell which child came from which side.","zh":"两个村子决定把各自的小学合并。老师们想把班级并在一起，用一条新路把两座旧校舍连起来。在两条路的交叉口，工人们修了一座宽门，一位木匠手工做了那两扇木门。两位校长每周一碰头商量这一周的安排。集市那天，两边的家庭都凑到台前看孩子们唱歌。两校合一并不容易，但现在没人分得清哪个孩子来自哪一边。"},"decide":{"tw":[["decision",4],["settle",0],["determine",2],["judge",3],["decisive",4],["rule",3],["resolve",0],["agree",6]],"en":"Our class had to decide where to spend the last school trip. The teacher said the decision must come from us. First we tried to settle the money problem, because that would determine everything else. Two students wanted the sea and three wanted the hills. We asked our teacher to judge which plan was fair. In the end his most decisive answer was simple: ask more people. When the vote was over we had to rule out the far places and resolve one last question about the bus. Everyone agreed.","zh":"我们班得决定最后一次班级旅行去哪儿。老师说这个决定必须由我们自己来做。我们先想办法解决钱的问题，因为那会决定其他一切。两个同学想去海边，三个想去山里。我们请老师来评判哪个方案更公平。最后他给出的最果断的回答很简单：多问些人。投票结束后，我们只能排除太远的地方，再解决最后一个关于大巴的疑问。所有人都同意了。"},"difference":{"tw":[["different",4],["differ",4],["differentiate",4],["conflict",0],["balance",3],["gap",3],["remainder",0],["quality",2]],"en":"The two reports about the same meeting were very different. They differ on one point only: the cost. Nobody could explain the difference, and soon it turned into a small conflict. My job was to check the balance of the two lists and find the gap between them. The remainder was small, but the quality of the work was not the same at all. In the end we had to differentiate between what we measured and what we guessed. That one difference changed the whole decision, and afterwards the two teams never worked in the same room again.","zh":"同一场会议的两份报告很不一样。它们只在一个点上不同：成本。没人能解释这个差异，很快它就变成了一场小冲突。我的工作是核对两张清单是否平衡，找出它们之间的缺口。剩余的部分很小，但工作的质量完全不同。最后我们不得不区分哪些是我们实测的、哪些是猜的。正是这一个差异改变了整个决定，此后两支队伍再也没在同一间屋里共事过。"},"judge":{"tw":[["judicial",4],["judiciary",4],["adjudicate",4],["guess",0],["decide",2],["try",0],["court",6],["jury",6],["think",2]],"en":"Nobody wanted to judge that case. The judicial system moves slowly here, and the judiciary in our town has only two small rooms. First the jury has to listen to both sides, then the judge has to decide. You cannot guess; you have to try every door and think about what is fair. To adjudicate a case like this takes weeks. Two old men sat at the back of the court all day and said nothing. When the decision finally came, the judge wrote three long pages, and everybody went home tired.","zh":"没人愿意审那个案子。这里的司法体系走得很慢，我们镇上的司法部门只有两间小屋。首先要由陪审团听双方陈述，然后由法官作出裁决。你不能靠猜，必须试遍每一条门路，想清楚什么是公平的。裁决这样一个案子要好几周。两个老人整天坐在法庭后排，一言不发。裁决终于下来时，法官写了三页长文，所有人都疲惫地回了家。"},"sense":{"tw":[["sensible",4],["sensitive",4],["sensor",4],["sensation",4],["feel",0],["smell",0],["detect",2],["understand",2],["logic",3]],"en":"There is a strange sensation in my left hand. I can feel the heat but I cannot feel the cold, and the doctor says the sensor in the skin has stopped working. It is still very sensitive to a light touch. I cannot smell the coffee any more either. The machine can detect the change, but nobody can understand it yet, and there is no logic in it. The doctors say the sense will come back slowly. A sensible person would rest at home, but I have work to do and my hands are the only tools I own.","zh":"我左手有一种奇怪的感觉。我能感觉到热，却感觉不到冷，医生说皮肤里的传感器已经不工作了。但它对轻微的触碰仍然很敏感。我也闻不到咖啡味了。仪器能检测到这个变化，却没人能解释，其中毫无逻辑可言。医生说这种感觉会慢慢恢复。明智的人会在家休息，可我还有活要干，而这双手是我唯一的工具。"},"enter":{"tw":[["entrance",4],["entry",4],["board",3],["exit",1],["record",0],["book",3],["figure",0],["leave",6]],"en":"You cannot enter the old hall through the front entrance any more. The entry in the book says the door was closed in 1974. If you want to go in, board the small bus at the gate and get off at the north exit; the guard will record your name in a thin notebook. I do not know the exact figure of visitors each year, but we never leave the place before six. The key is kept in a shop across the street, and the woman there will only give it to people she already knows.","zh":"你不能再从正门进入那座旧礼堂了。簿子上的记录说那扇门 1974 年就封了。想进去的话，在大门口坐上小巴，从北门下车，守卫会把你的名字记在一个薄本子里。我不知道每年访客的确切数字，但我们从不早于六点离开。钥匙存在街对面的一家店里，那位女士只把钥匙交给她认识的人。"},"form":{"tw":[["formation",4],["formative",4],["build",0],["class",0],["course",0],["body",2],["change",2]],"en":"The formation of a good habit takes months. My formative years were spent in a small school where the class was tiny and the course was fixed for the whole year. We had to build a routine and keep the body moving every morning before the bell. One small change in the order of things, and the whole form of the day falls apart. One winter our teacher was ill for a week, and everything we had built came apart in three days.","zh":"养成一个好习惯要花几个月。我的成长岁月是在一所小学校度过的，那里班级很小，课程整年都固定不变。我们得建立起一套作息，每天早晨铃响前让身体活动起来。只要顺序上有一点小改动，一整天的形态就散了。有一年冬天老师病了一周，我们建起来的那套东西三天就垮了。"},"head":{"tw":[["heady",4],["header",4],["lead",0],["mind",0],["control",2],["chair",3],["foot",1],["chief",6]],"en":"After two cups of that strong wine I felt heady and could hardly stand. My head was hot and my mind was not clear at all. Our chief engineer took control of the meeting, and the chair of the board sat at the end of the long table and did not lead the talk at all. A small header on the first page said 'Do not open'. From head to foot I felt the same strange heat, but nobody at the table seemed to notice; they drank water and went on working.","zh":"喝了两杯那种烈酒之后我觉得头晕，几乎站不住。我的头很热，脑子一点也不清楚。我们的总工程师掌控了会议，而董事会主席坐在长桌尽头，完全没有主导讨论。第一页上有一行小标题写着「请勿打开」。从头到脚我都感到同样奇怪的热，可桌上似乎没人察觉，他们喝着水继续干活。"},"heart":{"tw":[["hearty",4],["cardiac",4],["centre",0],["middle",0],["seat",3],["pain",6],["eye",0],["brain",6]],"en":"My grandfather had a cardiac problem last year. The doctor put a small machine in the centre of his chest, right in the middle, next to the heart. He still gets a pain in the left arm sometimes, but he eats a hearty breakfast and laughs a lot. His brain and his eye are fine, he says; it is only the seat of the trouble that is old. Every afternoon he walks to the end of the street and back, and the machine in his chest keeps the time for him.","zh":"我祖父去年心脏出了毛病。医生在他胸口正中央、紧贴心脏的位置放了一个小装置。他左臂有时还会痛，但他早餐吃得很香，也常笑。他说自己的脑子和眼睛都没问题，年久失修的只是毛病所在的那一处。每天下午他都走到街尾再折回来，胸里那个装置替他计着时间。"},"heat":{"tw":[["geothermal",4],["thermal",4],["cool",1],["cold",6],["temperature",6],["fry",3],["soak",3],["passion",0]],"en":"The geothermal water under this town is very hot. In winter we use it for the thermal baths, and the temperature stays near forty degrees all year. I like to soak in it for an hour, then run outside into the cold air to cool down. My friend cooks an egg in the steam and tries to fry bread on a flat stone. He has a passion for that sort of thing, and the heat never bothers him. In summer the same pipes carry cold water to every house on the street.","zh":"这个小镇地下的地热水很烫。冬天我们用地热浴室，水温全年保持在四十度左右。我喜欢在里面泡上一个小时，再跑到外面的冷空气里降温。我朋友在蒸汽里煮鸡蛋，还试着在一块平石上煎面包。他对这类事情极有热情，再热也从不介意。到了夏天，同一批管子给街上每户人家送冷水。"},"lay":{"tw":[["layer",4],["position",0],["pose",0],["load",3],["organize",2],["bare",6],["move",2],["hand",6]],"en":"We had to lay the old floor again. First we took off the top layer and put every board in the same position on the grass. The workers organize the load into two piles, and I help to hand them the nails. Do not move the wet ones, they say, they will crack in the sun. When the floor is bare, my sister likes to pose for a photograph there. I lay my hand on the cold stone underneath and rest, because the stone is older than the house itself.","zh":"我们得把旧地板重新铺一遍。先揭掉最上面一层，把每块木板按原样摆在草地上。工人们把货分成两堆，我帮忙递钉子。他们说湿的那些别动，太阳一晒会裂。地板露出来以后，我妹妹喜欢在那儿摆姿势拍照。我把手放在底下冰冷的石头上歇一会儿，因为那石头比房子本身还老。"},"line":{"tw":[["lining",4],["liner",4],["air",0],["blood",0],["business",0],["cover",2],["fill",2],["face",3]],"en":"There is a long line at the door of the shop every morning. The lining of my coat is torn, so I wear the old wool liner under it. People in the line talk about the air, about their blood pressure, about business. When the shop opens we fill the small room and cover the counter with our bags. I never see the same face twice. By nine the bread is always gone and the line simply disappears, as if it had never been there.","zh":"每天早上那家店门口都排着长队。我外套的衬里破了，所以里面套着一件旧羊毛内衬。排队的人聊空气、聊血压、聊生意。店门一开，我们就挤满那间小屋，把包堆在柜台上。我从来没见过重复的脸。到九点面包必定卖完，队伍就那样消失了，仿佛从没出现过。"},"picture":{"tw":[["depict",4],["pictorial",4],["photograph",0],["image",2],["illustrate",3],["figure",0],["film",0],["screen",6]],"en":"The picture on my wall is a photograph of the old harbour. It does not depict the whole town, only a small image of the boats. The book next to it is pictorial: every page has a drawing to illustrate one word. I like the figure of the boy in the corner best. In the film they showed last week, the same picture filled the whole screen for a few seconds. I bought it for almost nothing on a wet morning, and I have never wanted to sell it.","zh":"我墙上那幅画是一张旧港的照片。它没有描绘整个镇子，只有小船的一个小影像。旁边那本书是图解式的：每一页都有一幅画来解释一个词。我最喜欢角落里那个男孩的形象。在他们上周放的那部电影里，同一幅画面有几秒钟铺满了整个银幕。我是在一个雨天早晨几乎白捡来的，也从来没想卖掉它。"},"sight":{"tw":[["optic",4],["visual",4],["spectacle",3],["look",2],["position",2],["deal",0],["flood",3]],"en":"The sight from the top of the hill is famous. An optic company put a telescope there, and from that position you can see a visual trick: the sun seems to rise twice. A flood of light hits the valley below, and every look through the glass costs one coin. The whole spectacle lasts two minutes. People come from the next town to see it, and they never say a word while they wait. It is still a good deal for the money.","zh":"山顶上的景致很有名。一家光学公司在那里放了一台望远镜，从那个位置你能看到一个视觉上的把戏：太阳像是升起了两次。一大片光倾泻到下面的山谷，每看一次收一枚硬币。整个奇观持续两分钟。人们从邻镇赶来看，等待时一句话也不说。就这个价钱来说，仍然很划算。"},"sign":{"tw":[["signature",4],["signify",4],["mark",0],["flag",3],["write",2],["contract",0],["alarm",3],["house",0]],"en":"There was no sign on the door of the old house. The only mark I could find was a small flag on the gate and a name that somebody had been asked to write in pencil. The contract in my bag had a signature at the bottom, but I did not know what it was meant to signify. At six the alarm went off and we had to leave the room. Nobody came to explain, and the flag stayed on the gate for another twenty years.","zh":"那座老房子的门上没有任何标志。我能找到的唯一记号是大门上的一面小旗，还有一个被人用铅笔写下的名字。我包里那份合同底部有个签名，但我不知道它意味着什么。六点钟警报响了，我们只好离开那个房间。没人来解释，那面小旗又在门上挂了二十年。"},"stand":{"tw":[["standard",4],["stance",4],["base",0],["bear",0],["continue",2],["fight",2],["lie",1],["hold",6]],"en":"I cannot stand his stance on this question. The standard answer is to wait, but he wants to fight at once. His base is weak: he cannot bear the cost, and if he continues like this the whole plan will not hold. Everything he says seems to lie on one thin idea, and that idea is wrong. Two of his oldest friends left the room before he finished speaking. I stayed, because somebody has to tell him the truth. He will not thank me for it, but a friend who says nothing at all is not a friend.","zh":"我受不了他在这个问题上的立场。标准答案是等等看，可他想立刻开战。他的根基很弱：他承担不起这笔费用，再这样下去整个方案都撑不住。他说的每句话似乎都建立在一条单薄的想法上，而那条想法是错的。他还没说完，两个老朋友就离开了房间。我留了下来，因为总得有人告诉他真相。"},"star":{"tw":[["interstellar",4],["stellar",4],["sun",3],["ace",0],["champion",0],["idol",3],["character",2],["lead",0]],"en":"The star of our team is a quiet boy who never talks about his interstellar dreams. In the stellar light of the evening he runs faster than anyone else, and in the morning sun he trains alone before school begins. He is the ace of the school, our champion for three years, and the idol of every small child here. But his character is what I like most: he does not lead by shouting, and he never laughs at the slower boys.","zh":"我们队的明星是个安静的男孩，从不谈起自己星际旅行的梦想。傍晚的星光下他跑得比谁都快，清晨的太阳里他在开学前独自训练。他是学校的王牌、连续三年的冠军，也是这里每个小孩的偶像。但我最喜欢的是他的品性：他从不靠喊叫来带队，也从不嘲笑跑得慢的孩子。"},"tell":{"tw":[["tale",4],["teller",4],["say",0],["state",0],["express",2],["answer",3],["order",0],["know",6]],"en":"Let me tell you a short tale about a bank teller. He did not say much: he would state the amount, express nothing at all, and answer only yes or no. In order to understand the man you had to know his face. People tell me he was happy in that small room behind the thick glass. He never asked about my money and he never told me his name, but for ten years we said good morning to each other every day.","zh":"让我给你讲一个关于银行出纳员的短故事。他话不多：只报出金额，不流露任何情绪，回答也无非是或否。要理解这个人，你得熟悉他的表情。人们告诉我，他在那层厚玻璃后面的小屋里其实挺快乐。他从不打听我的钱，也从不告诉我他的名字，但十年来我们每天都互道早安。"},"trust":{"tw":[["trustee",4],["fiduciary",4],["believe",2],["hope",0],["credit",3],["count",3],["expect",2],["fund",6]],"en":"You cannot trust a trustee who never writes back. I still believe in him, and I hope he will return, but I do not expect it any more. The fund is small now, and the credit of the office is gone. You can count the people who still trust him on one hand; his fiduciary duty means nothing to the rest of us. His letters are still in my drawer, unopened, and I think they will stay there for a long time.","zh":"你没法信任一个从不回信的受托人。我仍然相信他，也希望他会回来，但我已经不抱期望了。基金现在很少，那间办公室的信誉也没了。还信任他的人一只手就数得过来；他的受托责任对其余的人来说毫无意义。他的信还放在我抽屉里，没有拆开，我想它们会在那里放很久。"},"wave":{"tw":[["waver",4],["wavy",4],["curl",0],["roll",0],["flap",3],["wake",3],["lift",3],["move",2]],"en":"A big wave hit the side of the boat. The wavy line of the water rose, curled and rolled over the deck. The sail began to flap and the wake behind us turned white. I did not move and I did not waver; the lift of the boat felt like a hand under my feet. An hour earlier the sea had been calm as a table, and by night it will be calm again. Only the rope in my hand says that any of this happened.","zh":"一个大浪打在船舷上。起伏的水线升起来，卷曲着翻过甲板。帆开始拍打，我们身后的尾迹变成了白色。我没有动，也没有动摇；船被托起来的感觉就像脚下有一只手。一小时前海面平得像桌面，到了夜里它又会平下来。只有手里这根绳子说明刚才的一切真的发生过。"},"word":{"tw":[["lexical",4],["verbal",4],["phrase",0],["book",0],["news",0],["express",2],["read",6],["order",2]],"en":"One word can change a whole page. I keep a lexical notebook: every verbal form and every short phrase goes into it. When I read the news I copy the words I do not know, in order of how often they appear. A book of ten thousand words is enough to express almost everything, my teacher says, and one wrong word can cost you a friend. I have filled four notebooks since I started, and the fifth is already half full with words I use every day.","zh":"一个词就能改变整页的意思。我有一本词汇笔记本：每个动词形式和每个短语都记进去。看新闻时我把不认识的词抄下来，按出现频率排序。我老师说，一本一万词的书足以表达几乎所有东西，而一个用错的词能让你失去一个朋友。开始记以来我已经写满四个本子。"},"death":{"tw":[["die",4],["dead",6],["mortuary",4],["end",2],["grave",3],["birth",1],["destruction",0],["demise",0]],"en":"The death of the old king changed everything. Few people died in the war itself, but the destruction of the city killed the trade. In the mortuary they counted the bodies, and the dead were carried out at dawn. The grave of his father stood next to the new one. His birth had been a feast; his demise was a silence, and the end came quietly. For a whole year afterwards the shops stayed shut and nobody sang in the streets.","zh":"老国王的死改变了一切。战争本身没死几个人，但城市的毁灭扼杀了贸易。在停尸房里他们清点遗体，死者于黎明时被抬走。他父亲的墓就在新墓旁边。他的出生曾是一场盛宴，他的离世却是一片寂静，结局来得悄无声息。此后整整一年，店铺都关着，街上再没人唱歌。"},"nose":{"tw":[["nosy",4],["nasal",4],["snout",3],["scent",0],["poke",0],["push",2],["throat",6],["front",2]],"en":"The dog has a cold nose and a very nasal bark. Its snout is always in the long grass, following some scent. Do not poke it and do not push it away; it will only come back. The hair on its throat is white, and the front of its face is black. My nosy neighbour says the dog knows everything that happens in this street. During the heat of the day it sleeps under the table and does not move at all.","zh":"那只狗鼻子凉凉的，叫声带着很重的鼻音。它的口鼻总埋在深草里，追着某种气味。别去戳它，也别把它推开，它只会再回来。它喉咙上的毛是白的，脸的前部是黑的。我那位爱打听的邻居说，这条街上发生的事这只狗全知道。白天最热的时候它就趴在桌子底下睡，一动也不动。"},"office":{"tw":[["official",4],["officiate",4],["position",0],["post",0],["headquarters",3],["duty",2],["staff",2],["department",6]],"en":"The office is on the third floor of an old building. The official letter says my position starts on Monday. Our headquarters is in another city, and this post is only a small department of four people. The staff are kind. My first duty is to answer the phone; I also have to officiate at the morning meeting. The lift has not worked since March, so we all take the stairs, and the stairs are the only place where anybody speaks freely.","zh":"办公室在一栋旧楼的三层。公函上说我的职位周一开始。我们的总部在另一个城市，这个岗位只是一个四人的小部门。同事们都很和气。我的第一项职责是接电话，还得主持晨会。电梯从三月起就坏了，所以我们全都走楼梯，而楼梯是唯一能让人畅所欲言的地方。"},"please":{"tw":[["pleasant",4],["pleasure",4],["delight",0],["satisfy",2],["enchant",3],["wish",2],["displease",1],["ask",6]],"en":"It is hard to please my aunt. A pleasant word in the morning will delight her, but nothing can satisfy her for long. The garden does not enchant her any more. I only wish she would ask for what she wants; then I could please her at once. Last week I displeased her by arriving late. It is no pleasure to sit in that room with her. She says the house is too quiet, and I think that is the whole trouble.","zh":"要让我姑妈满意很难。早上一句好听的话能让她高兴，但什么都不能让她满意太久。花园已经不再让她着迷了。我只希望她能把想要的东西说出来，那样我马上就能让她高兴。上周我迟到惹她不快。和她坐在那个房间里毫无乐趣可言。她说屋子太安静了，我想这就是全部的问题所在。"},"water":{"tw":[["aquatic",4],["hydraulic",4],["irrigate",0],["wet",2],["dry",6],["fill",2],["sand",6]],"en":"The water in this valley comes from a spring. In summer we irrigate the fields with it, and the hydraulic pump is old but still works. The aquatic plants near the edge stay wet all year, while the sand on the far side is dry. Every evening I fill two bottles and carry them home. In winter the spring slows down and we have to walk much further for the same two bottles. My mother says the spring has never once failed us, and I hope that is still true.","zh":"这个山谷里的水来自一眼泉。夏天我们用它灌溉田地，那台水泵很旧但还能用。靠边的水生植物终年是湿的，而远处那片沙子却是干的。每天傍晚我灌满两瓶水带回家。到了冬天泉水流得慢，为同样两瓶水我们得走远得多的路。"},"admit":{"tw":[["admission",4],["accept",2],["allow",0],["permit",2],["deny",1],["acknowledge",6],["seat",3],["serve",2]],"en":"They will not admit more than fifty people. The admission desk is at the door: if they accept your ticket they allow you in, but the permit is only for one hour. They deny nothing and acknowledge every question, yet the room can serve only a few at a time. I could not find a single empty seat. Outside, a hundred people were still waiting in the rain, and nobody there looked angry. They simply waited while the rain fell on their coats and on the stone steps of the hall.","zh":"他们最多只放进五十个人。售票处在门口：如果他们收下你的票就允许你进去，但许可只限一小时。他们什么也不否认，对每个问题都有回应，可那间屋子一次只能招待几个人。我一个空座位都没找到。外面还有一百个人在雨里等着，而那边没有一个人显得生气。"},"arm":{"tw":[["armament",4],["disarm",1],["weapon",0],["sword",3],["bow",3],["instrument",2],["limb",2],["finger",6]],"en":"He hurt his left arm in the factory last month. The limb was not broken, but he cannot lift a heavy instrument any more, and his fingers are slow in the cold. In the old armament room next door they keep weapons behind glass: a bow, a sword, two long guns. The guard had to disarm a man there once, and the story is still told in the village. My brother works with one hand now and laughs about it. He says a man only needs one good arm to do the work of two.","zh":"他上个月在工厂里伤了左臂。那条胳膊没断，但他再也不能举起重工具了，天冷时手指也不灵活。隔壁那间旧军械室里，武器都用玻璃罩着：一张弓、一把剑、两杆长枪。守卫曾在那里缴过一个人的械，这事村里至今还在讲。我哥哥现在只用一只手干活，还拿这事开玩笑。他说一个人只要有一条好胳膊，就能干两条胳膊的活。"},"better":{"tw":[["bet",4],["best",0],["improve",0],["worse",1],["change",2],["build",3],["break",0],["help",3]],"en":"I made a bet with myself last spring. The best way to get better at this job, I decided, is to build one small habit and never break it. A change of hours will help; working later only makes things worse. I want to improve slowly, not quickly. My brother says I should rest more, and I am sure he is right, because he is a good worker and I am not. So far I have kept the bet for eleven weeks, and the work is easier than it was.","zh":"去年春天我和自己打了个赌。我认定，要把这活儿做得更好，最好的办法是养成一个小习惯并且不打破它。改一改作息会有帮助；干到更晚只会让情况更糟。我要慢慢提高，而不是求快。我哥哥说我该多休息，我确信他是对的，因为他是个好工人而我不是。到现在这个赌我守了十一周，活儿也比从前轻松了。"},"home":{"tw":[["homely",4],["homestead",3],["house",2],["family",0],["return",2],["away",1],["lodge",3],["rest",6],["environment",2]],"en":"My idea of home is a homely room with one window. The house is small, but the homestead behind it has been in our family for four generations. When I return from the city I sleep for twelve hours; away from it I cannot rest at all. My friends lodge in a hotel two streets from here and say the environment is the same anywhere. I tell them they are wrong, and that one room you know is worth more than a big one you do not.","zh":"我心目中的家是一个带一扇窗的朴素房间。房子很小，可屋后那片宅地已属于我们家四代人了。从城里回来时我能睡上十二个小时；离开它我就完全无法休息。我的朋友们住在两条街外的一家旅馆，说环境在哪里都一样。我告诉他们他们错了，一间你熟悉的屋子比一间你不熟悉的大屋子值钱得多。"},"let":{"tw":[["letter",4],["allow",3],["accept",2],["prevent",1],["rent",0],["lease",0],["admit",3],["leave",2]],"en":"They will not let us sign the lease before June. The letter says the owner will allow three people in the flat, but he will not accept a dog. Nothing can prevent him from changing his mind either, and he will not admit that the price is too high. We rent the top floor now and pay by the week. If he decides to leave the country, we will have to find another place before the summer ends. The dog sleeps under the table in the kitchen and has never once barked at anybody.","zh":"他们不允许我们在六月前签租约。信上说房东允许三个人住这套公寓，但不接受养狗。也没什么能阻止他改主意，而他也不肯承认价格太高。我们现在租顶层，按周付钱。如果他决定出国，我们就得在夏天结束前另找住处。"},"light":{"tw":[["lightly",4],["clean",0],["clear",0],["flood",3],["surface",6],["dark",1],["burn",2],["match",3],["easy",5]],"en":"The light in this room is strange. It is clean and clear in the morning, when a flood of sun hits the white surface of the wall, but by four o'clock it is almost dark. I burn one candle and read by it, or I strike a match and walk to the window. Sleep comes lightly here; the dark does not feel heavy and the light does not hurt my eyes. It is easy to work in this room, and just as easy to stop working.","zh":"这屋子里的光很奇怪。清晨它干净而清澈，一大片阳光打在墙的白色表面上，可到四点就几乎黑了。我点一支蜡烛就着光读书，或者划根火柴走到窗前。在这里睡觉很浅；黑暗并不沉重，光也不刺眼。在这屋里很容易干活，也同样很容易就停下不干。"},"mind":{"tw":[["mental",4],["head",0],["tend",3],["forget",1],["manage",2],["worry",3],["notice",2],["idea",0],["listen",0]],"en":"There is too much in my mind this week. My head is full of small numbers, and I tend to forget names. The doctor says it is not a mental problem, only tiredness. I try to manage one thing at a time. Do not worry, she says, and notice what you eat. It is a good idea, and I should listen to her, but I never do. My mother had the same mind and the same habit of not listening to anybody.","zh":"这星期我脑子里装的东西太多了。我满脑子都是小数字，还容易忘名字。医生说这不是精神上的问题，只是累。我试着一次只处理一件事。别担心，她说，注意你吃的东西。这是个好主意，我该听她的，可我从来不听。我母亲也有同样的脑子，也有同样的、谁的话都不听的习惯。"},"notice":{"tw":[["notify",4],["bill",0],["knock",3],["sign",2],["ignore",1],["check",6],["card",0],["discover",0],["mention",3]],"en":"Did you notice the notice on the door? A small card says we must notify the office if we leave. Nobody told me about it; they did not even knock. There is a sign above the bell, but people ignore it every single day. I had to check the bill three times before I discovered the extra line at the bottom. When I asked about it, the man at the desk did not mention it once. He only looked at his hands.","zh":"你注意到门上那张告示了吗？一张小卡片说我们离开时必须通知办公室。没人跟我说过这件事，他们连门都没敲。铃上方有个标牌，可人们每天都视而不见。我把账单核对了三遍，才发现底部多出的那一行。我去问时，柜台后面那个人一次也没提。他只是看着自己的手。"},"pass":{"tw":[["passage",4],["clear",3],["break",3],["change",2],["fail",1],["carry",3],["leave",2],["draw",0]],"en":"You cannot pass this road in winter. The passage over the hill is clear for only three months, and one bad storm can break it completely. If the weather does not change, we will fail to reach the village at all. Two men carry the mail on foot and leave before dawn. I draw a map every year and it is never the same twice. Still, the post always gets through in the end, and that is the only thing that matters up here.","zh":"冬天你没法通过这条路。翻过山口那条通道只有三个月是通的，一场坏风暴就能把它彻底毁掉。如果天气不变，我们根本到不了那个村子。两个人徒步送信，天不亮就出发。我每年画一张地图，从来没重过样。可邮件最后总能送到，而在这山里那是唯一要紧的事。"},"present":{"tw":[["presence",4],["face",0],["date",3],["inform",2],["past",1],["stage",0],["state",2],["deliver",0]],"en":"At present there is no water in the tank. The presence of two engineers did not help; they only informed us of the date of the repair and left. On the stage above the door someone has written the state of the pump every day for ten years. In the past we never had to check it. The man who comes to deliver the parts knows the problem by heart, but he did not show his face for three days.","zh":"目前水箱里没有水。两位工程师在场也没用；他们只是通知了我们维修的日期就走了。门上方那块平台上，有人十年来每天都记下水泵的状态。从前我们根本不用检查。来送零件的那个人对这个问题了如指掌，可他整整三天没露面。"},"sound":{"tw":[["soundly",4],["voice",0],["acoustic",6],["noise",3],["silence",1],["heavy",0],["blow",3],["announce",2],["good",5]],"en":"The sound in the old hall is beautiful. A single voice fills it, and the acoustic roof holds every note. There is no noise from the street, only a heavy silence between the songs. When the singer stops you can hear the wind blow across the roof. The man at the door will announce the next piece in a low voice. At night the whole building sleeps soundly. It is a good place to sit and think, and nobody asks you to leave.","zh":"那座旧厅里的声音很美。一个人的嗓音就能填满它，声学屋顶留住了每一个音。街上没有噪音，歌声之间只有沉沉的寂静。歌手停下时，你能听见风掠过屋顶。门口那个人会用低沉的嗓音报出下一曲。夜里整栋楼睡得很沉。那是个适合坐着想事的好地方，也没人赶你走。"},"base":{"tw":[["basal",4],["bag",0],["bed",3],["bottom",2],["floor",0],["build",3],["control",2],["foot",0]],"en":"The base of the old tower is wider than the top. At the bottom there is a thick basal layer of stone, and below that only sand. We had to build a floor of wood over it so that nobody would fall through. Every bag of tools sits in the corner. From the control room you can see the whole valley, and it is a long way down to the foot of the hill. A bed of dry grass used to cover the stone, but the rain took it years ago.","zh":"那座古塔的基部比顶部宽。底部有一层很厚的基底石，再往下就只有沙子了。我们不得不在上面铺一层木地板，免得有人掉下去。每袋工具都堆在角落里。从控制室能看到整个山谷，往下到山脚还有很长一段路。从前有一层干草铺在石头上，但多年前就被雨水冲走了。"},"bet":{"tw":[["count",0],["pot",3],["trust",2],["raise",3],["gamble",2],["cash",6],["play",3],["better",4]],"en":"Do not bet on that horse. I do not trust the man who owns it, and I can count the times he has actually paid on one hand. The pot is small tonight, but he will raise it as soon as you sit down. My cousin likes to gamble and always plays with cash. You will feel better if you keep your money in your pocket. I learned that lesson in a single evening, and it was not a cheap one to learn.","zh":"别赌那匹马。我不信任它的主人，他真正付过钱的次数我一只手就数得过来。今晚的赌池很小，可你一坐下他就会加注。我表弟喜欢赌，而且总是用现金玩。把钱留在口袋里你会好受些。我是在一个晚上学会这个教训的，而那学费并不便宜。"},"board":{"tw":[["boarder",4],["card",0],["catch",3],["enter",2],["commission",6],["room",0],["deal",3],["table",2]],"en":"The board meets at eight. Each member puts a card on the table, and the chairman reads out the name of every boarder in the house. We deal with one question at a time, and only one. A small commission was set up last year to check the accounts, and nobody has entered that room since March. I try to catch the chairman before the meeting, but he is never alone. Last week they sat for four hours and decided nothing at all.","zh":"董事会八点开会。每位成员把一张卡片放在桌上，主席逐一念出屋里每位寄宿者的名字。我们一次只处理一个问题，而且只处理一个。去年成立了一个小委员会来查账，可自三月起没人进过那个房间。我想在会前逮住主席，可他从没落单过。上周他们坐了四个小时，什么也没定下来。"},"carry":{"tw":[["carriage",4],["bear",2],["deal",3],["act",2],["express",0],["fly",3],["bring",2],["hold",0]],"en":"I have to carry these boxes to the station. The carriage of the train leaves in an hour, and the porter will not bear more than two at a time. We deal with the heaviest first and then act quickly. If we are late they will not hold the train, and my sister will have to bring the rest tomorrow. The express never stops here. Nothing flies out of this town, so everything goes by rail. The porter says the same thing every winter, and every winter he turns out to be right.","zh":"我得把这些箱子搬到车站去。那趟火车的车厢一小时后开，搬运工一次不肯扛超过两箱。我们先处理最重的，然后动作要快。要是迟了他们不会等车，剩下的就得让我妹妹明天带来。快车从不停这里。这个镇上什么也飞不出去，所以一切都走铁路。"},"catch":{"tw":[["catchment",4],["see",0],["bag",3],["board",2],["stop",0],["fish",3],["throw",6],["view",0]],"en":"We could not catch a single fish all morning. The catchment above the dam is full of rain water and the fish are deep. I stood on the board and could not see a thing; my bag was still empty at noon. Then one careless throw of a stone by a boy on the far bank moved the whole shoal at once. From where I stood the view was lovely, but that does not stop me from wanting one fish. Next week I will try the other side, where the water is slower.","zh":"整个上午我们一条鱼也没抓到。水坝上游的集水区灌满了雨水，鱼都沉在深处。我站在木板上什么也看不见；到了中午我的袋子还是空的。后来一个男孩扔了块石头，整群鱼一下子全动了。从我站的地方看出去景色很美，可这并不能阻止我想要一条鱼。下周我要去另一边试试，那边水流更缓。"},"count":{"tw":[["counter",4],["bet",0],["total",3],["depend",0],["poll",3],["trust",2],["result",6],["look",0]],"en":"We count the votes twice. The counter at the front of the room is an old wooden table, and the total is written on the wall in chalk. You cannot depend on one count, and you cannot trust the first result either. At the last poll two hundred people came, and the look on his face said everything. I would bet the second count is the true one. Nobody argues after the second count; they simply pick up their coats and go home.","zh":"我们把票点两遍。屋子前面那张计数器是一张旧木桌，总数用粉笔写在墙上。你不能只靠一次计数，也不能相信第一次的结果。上一次投票来了两百人，而他脸上的表情说明了一切。我敢打赌第二次计数才是真的。第二次计数之后没人再争，他们只是拿起外套回家。"},"die":{"tw":[["death",4],["break",0],["fall",3],["change",2],["pass",0],["crash",3],["feel",2],["fail",0]],"en":"Old engines do not die all at once. First a small part breaks, then the pressure falls, and the change is very slow. You can feel it in the steering wheel months before the end. If the pump fails, the car will crash into the wall at the next bend. The death of an engine is a long story, and most of it happens quietly. Mine passed away on a Tuesday, in front of my own house, with the key still in the door.","zh":"老发动机不会一下子死掉。先是某个小零件坏掉，接着压力下降，变化非常慢。在结局到来前几个月，你就能在方向盘上感觉到。如果水泵失灵，车会在下一个弯道撞上墙。一台发动机的死亡是个漫长的故事，而且大部分是悄无声息地发生的。我那台是在一个星期二咽气的，就在我自己家门口，钥匙还插在门上。"},"doctor":{"tw":[["doctoral",4],["fix",0],["fill",3],["better",2],["nurse",6],["repair",0],["piece",3],["restore",0]],"en":"The doctor came at seven. He fixed my arm, filled a small cup with something bitter, and said I would feel better in a week. A nurse held the lamp; she said the same doctor had repaired her father's leg and restored it to full use. He showed me one small piece of bone in the palm of his hand. He is writing a doctoral paper about exactly this sort of injury. He told me I was lucky, and I did not argue with him.","zh":"医生七点来的。他给我接好了胳膊，倒了一小杯很苦的东西，说我一周后就会好些。一位护士举着灯；她说同一位医生修好过她父亲的腿，并让它完全恢复了功能。他摊开手掌给我看一小块骨头。他正在写一篇关于这类损伤的博士论文。他说我很幸运，我没有跟他争。"},"draw":{"tw":[["drawer",4],["force",0],["arrange",2],["match",6],["line",0],["catch",3],["win",6],["lot",0]],"en":"Let us draw for the first turn. In the drawer of the little table there are four cards; arrange them face down and each of us takes one. Catch your card before it falls on the floor. The match is won by the highest line, so look at it carefully. I never win anything by luck, and a lot of people at this table say the same. You can force the card if you want, but then there is no point in playing at all.","zh":"咱们抽签决定先手吧。小桌的抽屉里有四张牌；把它们正面朝下摆好，每人拿一张。牌掉到地上之前接住它。比赛由点数最大的那一行获胜，所以要看仔细。我从来没靠运气赢过什么，这张桌上很多人也这么说。你想的话可以硬来，但那样玩起来就没意思了。"},"drive":{"tw":[["drift",4],["cause",0],["lift",3],["fight",2],["force",0],["pull",3],["hit",2],["push",0]],"en":"It is a long drive to the coast. The road begins to drift west after the bridge, and the wind can cause the car to lift on the open bends. My father would push the speed up and then pull it back again; he never liked to fight the wheel. One year a stone hit the glass and we ran the last ten miles with no window at all. I drive slowly now, and the force of the wind still surprises me every time.","zh":"开车到海边要走很久。过了桥这条路就开始向西偏，在开阔的弯道上风能把车掀起来。我父亲会把速度推上去再收回来；他从不喜欢跟方向盘较劲。有一年一块石头打在玻璃上，我们最后十英里是没窗跑完的。我现在开得慢，而每次那股风力还是让我吃惊。"},"earth":{"tw":[["terrestrial",4],["ground",2],["floor",3],["concern",2],["space",6],["land",0],["forest",3],["hide",2],["world",0]],"en":"The earth here is red and thin. On the ground under the trees there is a soft floor of leaves, and the forest hides more than it shows. Scientists come to study the terrestrial plants; others look up at the space above the trees and forget the land under their feet. Their only concern is the rain, and the rain comes when it wants to. For me this small piece of earth is the whole world, and I do not want to leave it.","zh":"这里的土又红又薄。树下的地面上铺着一层松软的落叶，森林藏起来的比露出来的多。科学家来研究陆生植物；另一些人抬头看树顶以上的太空，却忘了脚下的土地。他们唯一关心的是雨，而雨想来就来。对我来说这一小块土地就是整个世界，我不想离开它。"},"edge":{"tw":[["edgy",4],["inch",0],["shoulder",3],["line",2],["march",0],["margin",3],["side",2],["border",3],["corner",6]],"en":"We walked along the edge of the field for an hour. The border with the next farm is only a line of small stones, and the margin of the wood lies on the far side. At the corner an old man was marching up and down with his shoulder against the wind. I moved an inch at a time, because the drop below was long. My friend felt edgy and would not look down once the whole way. We sat down at last, well back from the edge, and ate the bread we had brought.","zh":"我们沿着田边走了一个小时。与隔壁农场的分界只是一排小石头，树林的边缘在更远的一侧。拐角处有个老人顶着风来回踱步，肩膀迎着风口。我一次只挪一寸，因为下面的落差很大。我朋友一路上都很紧张，一次也没敢往下看。"},"face":{"tw":[["facial",4],["front",2],["bottom",3],["cover",2],["look",0],["top",3],["lie",2],["present",0]],"en":"I did not want to face him again. His face was in the front room, at the top of the stairs, and the look on it had not changed at all. He would not lie down and sat in the chair by the window all night. The bottom of the door was covered with old letters that nobody had opened. His facial expression was calm, too calm. At present I still do not know what I said to him that evening.","zh":"我不想再面对他。他的脸在前面那间屋里、楼梯顶端，脸上的表情一点没变。他不肯躺下，整夜坐在窗边那把椅子上。门的下半部堆满了没人拆过的旧信。他的面部表情很平静，平静得过分。直到现在我也不知道那天晚上我对他说了什么。"},"fire":{"tw":[["fiery",4],["burn",0],["bake",2],["hire",1],["raise",0],["excite",3],["explosion",6],["attack",2]],"en":"The fire started in the bakery at two. The old oven was still burning when we came, and the smell of baked bread was everywhere in the street. Someone raised the alarm, and the explosion of the gas bottle woke the whole neighbourhood. It was a fiery hour, and the thought of it still excites me. Nobody knows what could attack the wiring like that. They will not hire a new baker until the roof is fixed. The cat was found two streets away the next morning, asleep under a car.","zh":"火灾是两点在面包房起的。我们赶到时那个旧烤炉还在烧，街上到处是烤面包的味道。有人拉响了警报，煤气瓶的爆炸惊醒了整个街区。那是火光冲天的一小时，现在想起来还让我激动。没人知道是什么能那样侵蚀线路。屋顶修好之前他们不会雇新面包师。"},"fix":{"tw":[["fixture",4],["cook",0],["care",3],["better",2],["plug",6],["doctor",0],["dress",3],["hole",0]],"en":"Can you fix this lamp? The fixture is loose and the plug is broken. My brother cooked dinner while I worked, and my sister dressed the children and put them to bed. There is a hole in the wall behind the lamp that I cannot fill. The doctor who lived here before us took better care of this house than we ever did. I will fix it properly on Sunday. Until then we will sit in the dark and talk, which is not such a bad thing.","zh":"你能修一下这盏灯吗？灯具松了，插头也坏了。我干活时我哥哥做了晚饭，我姐姐给孩子们穿好衣服哄他们上床。灯后面墙上有个洞，我填不上。住在我们之前的那位医生对这房子比我们上心得多。我周日会好好修它。在那之前我们就摸黑坐着说话，这也算不上什么坏事。"},"green":{"tw":[["greenery",4],["park",0],["sprout",3],["site",2],["ripe",1],["emerald",3],["vegetable",2]],"en":"The green field behind the house turns yellow in July. The greenery along the river is thick, and in spring every small sprout comes up between the stones. We chose the site for the new park because it stays green all year. The emerald water below the bridge is cold, and the vegetable garden next to it is not ripe yet. My mother says green is the only colour she can trust. She has planted the same three rows for forty years.","zh":"屋后那片绿色的田到七月就变黄了。河边的草木很茂密，春天每一个小芽都从石缝里钻出来。我们把新公园选在这里，是因为它整年都是绿的。桥下那水呈翡翠色，很凉；旁边的菜园还没熟。我母亲说绿色是她唯一能信任的颜色。同一片三行地她种了四十年。"},"hand":{"tw":[["manual",4],["deal",3],["pass",0],["reach",0],["left",3],["right",3],["side",2],["hard",6]],"en":"Take my hand and do not let go. The manual says you must deal with the switch with your left hand only, and pass nothing to the other side of the machine. If you can reach the lever, pull it once and pull it hard. On the right there is a small wheel, and on the back a box of tools. My grandfather worked with either hand and never read a manual in his life. He says the hand knows more than the head, and for this job he is right.","zh":"抓住我的手，别松开。手册上说，操作这个开关只能用左手，而且不能把任何东西递到机器的另一侧。如果你够得到那根杠杆，就拉一次，用力拉。右边有个小轮子，后面有个工具箱。我祖父两只手都能干活，一辈子没读过手册。他说手比脑子懂得多，干这活儿他说得对。"},"lock":{"tw":[["locker",4],["curl",0],["engage",0],["hold",2],["hook",6],["mesh",0],["hair",2],["prop",6]],"en":"The lock on the old locker is broken. Inside there is a rope, a metal hook and a piece of mesh that used to hold the window shut. You have to engage the small lever first, then turn the key twice, and only then will the prop stay in place. My sister's hair was caught in it once, in a single curl, and she has never touched the door since. I keep a spare key in my pocket for the days when it refuses to open.","zh":"那个旧储物柜的锁坏了。里面有一根绳子、一个金属钩子，还有一块以前用来顶住窗户的铁丝网。你得先把小杠杆卡上，然后把钥匙转两圈，这样撑杆才待得住。我姐姐的头发曾被卷进去过一缕，从那以后她再没碰过那扇门。我在口袋里放了一把备用钥匙，专对付它打不开的日子。"},"mouth":{"tw":[["oral",4],["lip",0],["shout",3],["tongue",6],["speak",0],["sing",3],["communicate",2],["talk",0]],"en":"Keep your mouth closed when you chew. The oral exam next week will test how you open a speech, and my teacher wants us to speak slowly. When you shout, the tongue moves differently than when you sing. She says a mouth can talk all day and communicate nothing at all. Her lower lip is dry and her voice is thin now. Do not touch the microphone with your lips. My mother puts a finger to her lips whenever I open mine at the table.","zh":"嚼东西的时候把嘴闭上。下周的口试要考你怎么开头演讲，老师要我们说慢一点。喊的时候，舌头的动作和唱歌时不一样。她说一张嘴能说一整天却什么也没表达。她的下唇很干，嗓音如今也细弱了。别用嘴唇碰麦克风。"},"move":{"tw":[["motion",4],["act",2],["beat",3],["cause",2],["continue",6],["run",0],["begin",3],["change",2]],"en":"We have to move the piano before Friday. The motion of the truck on these roads will damage it, so we wrap every leg in cloth. I cannot act alone; two people have to lift at the same time, to the same beat. Nothing will cause more trouble than the stairs. If it starts to rain we will begin again in the morning. Water can change the shape of wood in one night, so we cannot stay outside. The whole move should take two hours if nobody runs. We will continue with the small boxes indoors.","zh":"我们得在周五前把钢琴搬走。卡车在这些路上的颠簸会把它弄坏，所以我们把每条腿都裹上布。我一个人做不了；两个人得同时抬，按同一个节拍。没有比那几级楼梯更麻烦的了。要是下起雨来，我们就第二天早上重来。水一夜之间就能改变木头的形状，所以不能放在外面。只要没人乱跑，整个搬运两小时就能完。"},"name":{"tw":[["nominal",4],["call",0],["refer",6],["discover",0],["raise",3],["appoint",2],["family",2],["figure",0]],"en":"Nobody knows the real name of the old man at the gate. People call him 'the captain', but that is only a nominal title; nobody has been able to discover where it came from. His family name is carved above the door, and I have to refer to it every morning when I raise the flag. The committee will appoint a new watchman in June. The figure of a woman on the gate carries the same name. Even the map of the town carries the same name in its corner. It has been there since 1893, and nobody has ever tried to change it.","zh":"没人知道大门口那位老人的真名。大家叫他「船长」，可那只是个名义上的称呼；没人能查清它的来历。他的姓氏刻在门楣上，我每天早上升旗时都得提到它。委员会六月要任命一名新看守。大门上那个女人的雕像也带着同一个名字。"},"need":{"tw":[["needy",4],["ask",0],["want",0],["demand",0],["cost",3],["condition",2],["poverty",2],["cry",3]],"en":"Tell me what you need. Do not ask twice and do not demand; just say it once. The cost of the repairs is small, but the condition of the roof is not, and sooner or later we will have to deal with it. There are two needy families in this street, and one of them lives in real poverty. I heard a child cry last night, in the house at the corner. I am sure they want nothing more than a warm room.","zh":"告诉我你需要什么。别问两遍，也别强求，说一次就够了。修理的花费不大，可屋顶的状况不好，迟早得处理。这条街上有两户穷苦人家，其中一户真的是一贫如洗。昨晚我听见一个孩子在哭，就在拐角那栋房子里。我敢肯定，他们想要的不过是一间暖和的屋子。"},"note":{"tw":[["annotate",4],["bill",0],["quote",6],["line",0],["mark",0],["read",6],["state",2],["excuse",3]],"en":"I left a note on the table. It says the bill has been paid and the spare key is under the pot. I had to annotate the last page, because the small line at the bottom is easy to miss. Do not quote me on any of this, and do not read the note to the king; he will only look for an excuse. The state of the accounts is written in the same note, and I put a mark next to every name.","zh":"我在桌上留了张字条。上面写着账单已经付了，备用钥匙在花盆底下。最后一页我不得不加注，因为底下那一小行很容易看漏。这些话别引我的话，也别把字条念给国王听，他只会找个借口。账目状况也写在同一张字条上，我在每个名字旁都做了记号。"},"nurse":{"tw":[["nursery",4],["hold",0],["midwife",3],["care",2],["entertain",0],["matron",3],["feed",2],["nanny",0]],"en":"The nurse comes at six and the matron at eight. In the nursery next door there are twelve small beds, and a nanny feeds the smallest ones by hand. The midwife who delivered my brother still works here; she says care is the only medicine that never runs out. I hold the lamp for her while she works. She will entertain the children for an hour and then send them all to bed. In the winter she stays until midnight, and nobody asks her to. The children call her by her first name, which the matron does not like at all.","zh":"护士六点来，护士长八点来。隔壁的育婴室里摆着十二张小床，一位保姆用手一口口喂最小的那几个。当年接生我弟弟的助产士如今还在这儿干；她说照护是唯一永远不会用完的药。她干活时我替她举着灯。她会陪孩子们玩一个小时，然后把他们全都打发上床。"},"position":{"tw":[["posit",4],["lay",0],["dress",3],["move",2],["office",0],["face",3],["state",2],["post",0]],"en":"My position in the office is a small one. I lay out the letters in the morning and move the files from one post to another. The face of the building is being repaired, so we dress the windows with paper. I would posit that nobody here knows what the final state of the plan will be. However, we will keep working. The sign on the door still carries the old name. Every day I do the same three things, and every day they take the same time. My desk is by the window, and I can see the river from it.","zh":"我在办公室里的职位很小。早上我把信件摊开，把文件从一个岗位挪到另一个岗位。大楼的正面正在维修，所以我们用纸把窗户糊起来。我敢假定这里没人知道这个计划最终的状态是什么。不管怎样，我们还会继续干。门上的牌子还挂着旧名字。"},"post":{"tw":[["poster",4],["carry",0],["express",3],["call",2],["press",6],["office",0],["locate",3],["list",2],["position",0]],"en":"Every post brings two letters and a newspaper. The office cannot locate the missing parcel, and nobody can tell me which list it is on. I put a poster on the wall: 'Do not post cash'. We carry the bags to the express box before nine, and the press calls us every afternoon, sometimes twice. My position here is simple: I sort the mail and I keep quiet. At Christmas the bags are so heavy that two of us have to carry them. Nobody writes letters any more, they say, but the bags are never lighter.","zh":"每一班邮件送来两封信和一份报纸。办公室查不到那个丢失的包裹，也没人告诉我它在哪张清单上。我在墙上贴了张海报：「勿寄现金」。九点前我们把邮袋送到快递箱，报社每天下午都打电话来，有时打两次。我在这里的岗位很简单：分拣邮件，闭嘴干活。"},"race":{"tw":[["run",0],["heat",3],["act",2],["contest",6],["wash",0],["tear",3],["move",2],["rush",0]],"en":"The race begins at noon. Nobody can act as if it is only a game: the heat of the day will decide half of it. We watch from the bank, where the water can wash the mud off our shoes. A hundred people run, and the crowd cannot move at all when the rush starts at the first corner. This contest is older than the town. One year the wind was strong enough to tear every flag off the poles.","zh":"比赛中午开始。谁也不能装作这只是一场游戏：当天的暑气会决定一半的胜负。我们在河岸上看，那里的水能洗掉鞋上的泥。一百个人在跑，第一个弯道拥挤开始时，人群根本动不了。这项比赛比镇子还老。有一年风大得把所有旗子都从杆子上扯了下来。"},"sing":{"tw":[["song",4],["talk",2],["chant",3],["sound",2],["tune",6],["whistle",0],["hum",3],["listen",6],["interpret",2]],"en":"Please sing that song again. My grandmother could talk about music for hours; she said every tune has a sound of its own. In the old church they chant without a book, and the children hum along. When I was small I could only whistle, never sing. I listen to the same three songs every winter, and each time I interpret the words a little differently. The last line is always the same, and that is why I remember it. If you want, we can sing it together on Sunday evening.","zh":"请把那首歌再唱一遍。我祖母谈起音乐能说上几个小时；她说每支曲子都有自己独特的声音。在那座旧教堂里，人们不看谱子吟唱，孩子们跟着哼。我小时候只会吹口哨，从不会唱。每年冬天我都听同样的三首歌，而每一次我对歌词的理解都略有不同。"},"skin":{"tw":[["skinny",4],["bark",0],["scalp",3],["hide",0],["jacket",3],["bag",2],["breast",6],["struggle",0],["climb",2]],"en":"The skin on his hands is hard and dark. He is skinny now, and his jacket hangs loose on him. A leather bag, made from the hide of an old cow, sits on the floor next to his boots. The bark of the tree outside is rough, like his scalp. He has a mark on his breast, near the throat, from a struggle twenty years ago. Every winter he has to climb the same hill twice a day. He says the cold has taken the feeling out of it, and he does not miss it.","zh":"他手上的皮肤又硬又黑。他如今很瘦，夹克挂在身上空荡荡的。一个用老牛皮做的皮包放在地上，挨着他的靴子。外面那棵树的树皮很粗糙，就像他的头皮。他胸口靠近喉咙处有一道疤，是二十年前一场扭打留下的。每年冬天他都得每天爬两次那座山。"},"speak":{"tw":[["speech",4],["address",0],["sound",2],["listen",6],["mouth",0],["shout",3],["communicate",2],["continue",3]],"en":"I cannot speak in front of a crowd. My speech was ready, but when I stood up my mouth went dry and the sound of the room was louder than my voice. People began to shout from the back. I tried to continue and then to address one man only. It is easier to listen than to speak, and much easier to keep quiet. Next time I will try to communicate something shorter. My hands shake when the room is quiet, and they shake even more when it is not.","zh":"我无法在人前讲话。讲稿早就写好了，可我一站起来嘴就发干，屋里的声音比我的嗓音还大。后面的人开始喊。我试着继续说下去，接着只对着一个人讲。听比说容易，闭嘴不说更容易。下次我要试着讲短一点。"},"state":{"tw":[["civil",4],["country",0],["propose",2],["express",2],["answer",3],["attribute",2],["law",6],["land",0],["add",3]],"en":"The state of the roads is the main question here. Our country has a new law about land, and the administration wants to add three more. I cannot propose anything better: no state can express what the farmers feel when the water comes. You can attribute the damage to the rain, but that is not the answer. The civil servants came, wrote one page and left. Every spring we wait for them to come back. The old man who keeps the records says the state of things was worse in his father's day.","zh":"道路的状况是这里的主要问题。我们国家有了一项关于土地的新法律，行政部门还想再加上三条。我提不出更好的办法：没有什么状态能表达农民在水来时的感受。你可以把损失归因于雨水，可那不是答案。公务员来了，写了一页纸就走了。每年春天我们都等着他们再回来。"},"study":{"tw":[["student",4],["consider",0],["check",3],["research",6],["field",0],["major",3],["think",2],["learn",2]],"en":"I study in the room above the shop. There is one small window and a table full of books. My sister is a student of science; she comes here to research the plants in the field behind the house. We check each other's work every evening. I think this is the only way to learn: consider one thing at a time and then leave it alone. Her major is much harder than mine. My father studied in the same room and never got further than the second book. He says a good table is worth more than a good teacher.","zh":"我在店铺楼上那间屋里学习。屋里只有一扇小窗和一张堆满书的桌子。我妹妹是学理科的学生；她到这里来研究屋后地里的植物。每天晚上我们互相检查作业。我想这是唯一的学习方法：一次只琢磨一件事，然后就放手。她的专业比我的难得多。"},"tie":{"tw":[["draw",0],["ground",3],["finish",2],["marry",0],["join",3],["relate",2],["round",6],["attach",3],["straight",6]],"en":"He wore a black tie to the wedding. The two families will join their names, and after the ceremony they will marry in the old church, on the ground floor of which his mother was born. I had to finish the flowers before nine and attach a card to each one. It is hard to relate one thing to another here. We sat round the table and nobody could draw a straight line. The knot took me ten minutes, and in the photograph it is still crooked. My mother laughed at me and tied it again in one movement.","zh":"他打了条黑领带去参加婚礼。两家人要合成一个姓，仪式之后他们将在那座老教堂里成婚——他母亲就出生在那教堂的底层。我得在九点前把花弄完，并在每一束上别一张卡片。在这里很难把一件事和另一件事联系起来。我们围着桌子坐着，没人能画出一条直线。"},"time":{"tw":[["clock",0],["dead",3],["experience",2],["clip",0],["hour",3],["term",2],["next",6],["sentence",0]],"en":"We have no time, and the clock on the wall is dead. It stopped at five past four one afternoon in June, and nobody has touched it since. Experience tells me the next hour will decide everything. The term ends on Friday, and my last sentence has to be in by then. I will clip the papers together and hand them over at the door. It is the same every year. I have written the date on every page so that I will know the time of it later. Someday someone will read these pages and count the days between them.","zh":"我们没有时间，而墙上的钟是停的。它在六月的一个下午四点零五分停了，此后没人碰过它。经验告诉我，接下来的一个小时会决定一切。学期周五结束，到那时我最后一句必须交上去。我会把纸夹在一起，在门口交出去。每年都是这样。"},"touch":{"tw":[["tactile",4],["concern",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["easy",6],["meet",0],["cover",3],["change",2],["reach",0]],"en":"Do not touch the glass. The tactile map behind it is for blind visitors, and every finger leaves a mark. I have one small concern: the cover of the case is loose. It is easy to change the paper, but you must act before the glue dries. We will meet on Thursday and catch up on the rest. The hand of the woman in the picture is reaching for the same door. The guard watches everybody's hands, and nobody has ever touched the glass twice. He stands there all day and says nothing at all.","zh":"别碰玻璃。后面那张触摸地图是给盲人访客用的，每根手指都会留下印子。我有一个小顾虑：盒子的盖子松了。换纸很容易，但必须在胶干之前动手。我们周四见面，把剩下的部分跟上。画里那个女人的手也正伸向同一扇门。"},"try":{"tw":[["trial",4],["hear",0],["best",3],["act",2],["bring",6],["judge",0],["control",3],["taste",0]],"en":"I will try once more, and then I will stop. The trial next week is about a small house near the river, and the judge has asked me to bring the old papers. We will hear the first witness on Monday. Nothing here is under my control; the best I can do is act quickly and taste the food before I serve it. There is a pain in my back that will not go away. My sister says I should give up, and I tell her that trying is all I have.","zh":"我再试一次，然后就停下。下周的庭审涉及河边一栋小房子，法官要我把旧文件带过去。周一会听第一位证人陈述。这里没有一件事在我掌控之中；我能做的最好的事就是动作快一点，上菜前先尝一口。我背上有一处疼痛怎么也不消。"},"type":{"tw":[["typify",4],["character",0],["breed",3],["write",2],["example",6],["eccentric",0],["shift",3],["adult",2]],"en":"What type of dog is that? The breed is old and rather eccentric: it will typify the whole group in every show. Its character is calm, and the adult dogs sleep all day. I have to write four pages about this type of animal, with an example of each. The night shift begins at ten, and the same man has worked it for years. He says he knows every type by its bark alone. There are forty types in the book, and I have to describe every one of them.","zh":"那是什么品种的狗？这品种很老，也相当古怪：每到比赛它都能代表整组狗的特点。它的性情温和，成年的狗整天睡觉。我得写四页讲这类动物，每一类都要举一个例子。夜班十点开始，同一个人已经干了好几年。他说只听叫声就能认出每一种。"},"use":{"tw":[["usage",4],["employ",0],["apply",0],["drink",3],["demand",2],["require",6],["exercise",0],["board",3],["act",2]],"en":"The use of this room is written on the board. You may employ the machine for two hours a day, but you have to apply in writing first. The usage is strict: no drink near the desk. Older people require a chair and will demand one. We exercise every morning before the doors open, and the act of standing up is the hardest part. Nobody has ever asked me what the machines are for. The man who wrote the rules retired in 1990 and has not been back since. Everyone here knows the rules, and nobody has ever read them.","zh":"这间屋子的用途写在牌子上。你每天可以用这台机器两小时，但得先书面申请。规矩很严：桌边不许喝饮料。年纪大的人需要椅子，而且会开口要。每天早上开门前我们做操，而站起来这个动作是最难的一环。从没有人问过我这些机器是干什么用的。"},"wait":{"tw":[["waiter",4],["expect",3],["extension",3],["act",2],["stay",6],["hold",0],["ambush",3],["look",0]],"en":"We had to wait two hours for a table. The waiter told us to expect another twenty minutes, and then another. My sister could not stay; she had work to do. I left my name at the extension desk and sat in the corner, where I could look at the door. The ambush in the book I was reading lasted three pages. I had to hold the book with both hands, it was so cold. When the table was ready at last, my sister had already gone home. The waiter said the delay was nobody's fault, but every act of service in that place takes an hour.","zh":"我们等位子等了两个小时。服务员说再等二十分钟，然后又二十分钟。我妹妹待不住，她还有活要干。我把名字留在分机台，坐到角落里，从那儿能看见门口。我读的那本书里，一次伏击写了三页。我不得不用两只手抱着书，实在太冷了。"},"wall":{"tw":[["mural",4],["fence",2],["gable",3],["surround",0],["parapet",3],["layer",2],["floor",6],["object",2],["street",6]],"en":"There is a wall around the old garden. On the inside, the mural above the door shows the whole history of the street. The parapet is broken in two places, and a wooden fence covers the gap. Every layer of paint on the wall belongs to a different year. The gable of the house next door leans over it, and on the floor near the gate somebody has left a heavy object. The wall will surround this garden long after we are gone.","zh":"老花园四周有一道墙。墙内侧、门上方那幅壁画讲着这条街的整部历史。墙头有两处塌了，用一道木栅栏挡着缺口。墙上每一层漆都属于不同年份。隔壁房子的山墙朝它倾斜过来，大门附近的地上有人撂下了一个很重的东西。等我们都不在了，这道墙还会围着这座花园。"},"weight":{"tw":[["weighty",4],["burden",0],["load",3],["charge",2],["maximum",6],["bias",2],["excess",6],["angle",0]],"en":"The weight of the box was more than I expected. It is a weighty thing, and the burden of carrying it up the stairs fell on my brother. The maximum load for the old lift is eighty kilos, so we had to go on foot. He put it on the table at an angle and said the charge would be extra. There is a bias in the way we measure these things: two men always say a box is lighter than one man does. The excess goes back to the yard, where the same two men will argue about the angle of the ramp.","zh":"那个箱子比我想的重。它很沉，搬上楼的担子就落在我哥哥身上。这部旧电梯的最大载重是八十公斤，所以我们只好走楼梯。他把箱子斜着放在桌上，说搬运要另收费。我们衡量这些东西时是有偏见的：两个人总说箱子比一个人说的要轻。"},"book":{"tw":[["booking",4],["hold",0],["card",3],["register",2],["novel",6],["record",2],["ticket",3],["essay",6]],"en":"I read one book about the sea every winter. It is not a novel; it is the record of a man who worked on a boat for thirty years. He could not hold a pen at first, so his wife wrote the booking of every trip in a register and kept a ticket from each town they came to. The card inside the cover is my grandfather's, and the essay at the back was written by a schoolboy. Every page is thin and dry, and the words on them have lasted much longer than the boat did.","zh":"每年冬天我都读一本关于海的书。那不是小说，而是一个在船上干了三十年的人的记录。他起初握不住笔，所以他妻子把每次出航的登记都写进一本登记簿，还留下他们到过的每个城镇的船票。封面里那张卡片是我祖父的，后面那篇文章是一个小学生写的。"},"case":{"tw":[["casing",4],["cause",0],["box",3],["problem",2],["trial",6],["slip",0],["face",0],["pack",3]],"en":"In this case there is no easy answer. The problem is not the box; it is the casing inside it, which is thin. Nobody can find the cause. At the trial the judge asked for a slip of paper with the numbers on it, and my face gave me away. I had to pack the whole thing again and take it home on the bus. The next case on the list was even worse. Two weeks later a man came to the door with the same box and asked me the same question again.","zh":"这个案子里没有简单的答案。问题不在箱子，而在里面那层很薄的壳体。没人找得出原因。开审时法官要一张写有数字的纸条，而我的脸色把我出卖了。我只好把东西重新打包，坐公交带回家。清单上的下一个案子更糟。"},"class":{"tw":[["classify",4],["course",0],["count",3],["league",2],["standard",6],["family",0],["rank",6],["form",0]],"en":"Our class has twenty-two children in it. The teacher has to classify them by age and by reading level, and the standard of the older ones is not much higher. We play in a small league on Saturdays, and my rank in the group is fourth. The course lasts one year. The form of the test has changed twice since I came. In my family nobody finished school, so I count myself lucky to be here at all. The teacher says a good class is not a list of names but a habit of working that lasts for years.","zh":"我们班有二十二个孩子。老师得按年龄和阅读水平给他们分类，而大孩子的水平并不高多少。我们周六参加一个小联赛，我在组里的名次是第四。课程为期一年。我入学以来考试的形式已经改过两次。我们家没人读完过中学，所以我觉得自己能在这儿已经很幸运了。"},"country":{"tw":[["rural",4],["land",0],["open",3],["region",2],["nation",0],["state",0],["far",6],["space",3]],"en":"I grew up in the country, in a rural region where the land is cheap and the roads are empty. Our nation has eight such regions, and the state pays for the schools in all of them. The open field behind our house is the only space the children have. The nearest town is far; my aunt says it takes an hour if the wind is against you. In summer the whole country smells of cut grass. The government sends one bus a week, and the driver knows every family in the valley by name.","zh":"我在乡下长大，那是个土地便宜、道路空旷的农业地区。我们国家有八个这样的地区，所有地区的学校都由政府出资。屋后那片开阔的田是孩子们仅有的空间。最近的镇子很远；我姑妈说，要是逆风得走一个小时。夏天整个乡下都是青草被割过的味道。"},"father":{"tw":[["paternal",4],["mother",1],["patriarch",3],["head",2],["grandfather",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["engender",0]],"en":"My father was born in a house that no longer exists. His paternal grandfather, an old patriarch, was the head of a family of eleven. My mother says the two of them could generate an argument out of nothing, and that noise would engender more noise. Every parent in that street knew everybody else's business. My father never spoke of it, and I only learned the whole story from my aunt. My mother kept a photograph of the old house in a drawer for forty years, and then it was lost.","zh":"我父亲出生在一栋如今已不存在的房子里。他父系那边的祖父，一位老家长，是十一个人大家庭的户主。我母亲说那两个人能凭空吵出一场争论，而那吵闹又会生出更多吵闹。那条街上每对父母都知道别人家的私事。我父亲从不提这些，整个故事我还是从我姑妈那儿听来的。"},"flower":{"tw":[["floral",4],["bloom",0],["bud",3],["develop",2],["tree",6],["prime",0],["daisy",3],["garden",6]],"en":"The flower show opens on the first Saturday of June. Every garden in the village brings something: one rose, one daisy, one strange plant in a pot. The floral tent is the biggest in the county. My aunt watches her buds for weeks; a flower that is not yet in bloom cannot win, and one past its prime cannot either. The tree by the gate develops its leaves late and loses them early. The judge looks at the colour first and the shape last, and he never hurries. The show closes at six and the tent is taken down the same evening.","zh":"花展六月的第一个周六开幕。村里每座园子都拿出点什么：一支玫瑰、一朵雏菊、一盆奇怪的植物。那座花卉帐篷是全县最大的。我姑妈守着花苞看了好几周；还没开的花赢不了，过了盛期的也赢不了。大门边那棵树发芽晚，落叶却早。"},"number":{"tw":[["numeric",4],["square",3],["company",2],["total",3],["count",0],["several",6],["least",6],["bit",0]],"en":"Write your number at the top of the page. The system is numeric: no letters, no dashes. Our company counts every call, and the total last month was a little over nine hundred. Several of them were wrong. A square of paper with the same number is pinned to the board. I am tired, and it takes the least bit of noise to make me lose the count. The office has a number for everything: the door, the phone, the pile of paper on the shelf. I write mine on the back of my hand so that I will not forget it.","zh":"把号码写在页面顶端。格式是纯数字：不要字母，不要短横。我们公司统计每一通电话，上个月的总数略超九百。其中有几通是错的。一张写着同样号码的方纸钉在告示板上。我累了，一点点响声就能让我数乱。"},"school":{"tw":[["scholastic",4],["educate",2],["conservatory",3],["college",6],["train",0],["swim",2],["graduate",6],["civilise",0]],"en":"The school stands at the end of the street. Its scholastic record is not famous, but it has educated half the village. There is a conservatory behind it where the children train in music, and a small pool where they swim in summer. My sister went on to college and will graduate in July. Nobody here speaks of civilising anybody; they only want the children to be able to read. The building is old, and the roof was repaired with money the parents collected themselves. Every year the oldest children repaint the front wall before the summer.","zh":"学校坐落在街的尽头。它的学业成绩并不出名，却教出了半个村子的人。后面有个玻璃琴房，孩子们在那里练音乐；还有个小水池，夏天他们在里面游泳。我妹妹后来上了大学，七月就要毕业。这里没人说什么开化谁，他们只想让孩子能读书。"},"simple":{"tw":[["simplicity",4],["bare",0],["square",3],["complex",1],["perfect",6],["mere",0],["fool",3],["straightforward",6]],"en":"The answer is simple. The plan has a kind of simplicity that fools people: a bare room, one square table, one chair. Any honest worker would call it straightforward. The truth is that it is not complex, and it is not perfect either. It is elementary, and only a fool would try to improve it. My father built the whole thing in a single week, and it still stands. For a mere fifty pounds we could make it better, but nobody wants to spend the money. So we leave it as it is, and it works.","zh":"答案很简单。这个方案有一种会骗人的简洁：一间空屋、一张方桌、一把椅子。任何老实的工人都会说这很直白。事实是它不复杂，也不完美。它很基础，只有傻子才会想去改进它。我父亲用一周就把它全做出来了，而它至今还立在那儿。"},"space":{"tw":[["spatial",4],["blank",0],["hole",3],["distance",0],["infinite",0],["shuttle",6],["key",3],["earth",6]],"en":"There is no space left in the cupboard. A hole in the wall behind it gives us a little more, and the distance from there to the window is about a metre. In the city the shuttle bus comes every ten minutes. My teacher says space is infinite and the earth is not, and then he draws a blank on the board. The key to the whole problem is spatial: it is about where things are, not what they are.","zh":"柜子里没地方了。它后面墙上的一个洞给了我们一点余地，从那儿到窗户的距离大约一米。在城里，穿梭巴士每十分钟一班。我老师说空间是无限的，而地球不是，然后他在黑板上画了个空白。整个问题的关键在于空间：它关乎东西在哪里，而不是它们是什么。"},"suppose":{"tw":[["supposition",4],["guess",0],["suspect",3],["assume",2],["premise",3],["presume",6],["imagine",0],["say",0]],"en":"I suppose you have heard the story. It is a supposition, nothing more; nobody can say where it began. I suspect the first man only wanted to make us guess. Do not assume that the premise is true, and do not presume that I know either. Imagine a village where nobody had ever left, and you will understand why the story grew. That is the whole of it. I have told it to my children exactly as it was told to me, without adding anything. They will tell it to theirs, and the supposition will be the same.","zh":"我猜这个故事你听过。它只是一个推测，仅此而已；没人说得出它从哪儿开始。我怀疑最初那个人只是想让我们猜。别认定那个前提是真的，也别以为我就知道。想一想一个从没有人离开过的村子，你就会明白这故事为什么会越传越大。事情就是这样。"},"term":{"tw":[["terminal",4],["condition",0],["subject",3],["word",2],["current",6],["terminus",0],["predicate",3],["quantity",2]],"en":"The term ends in three weeks. In this subject the predicate carries most of the meaning, and one wrong word can change the whole sentence. The quantity of reading is small; the interest is not. I stand at the bus terminal every morning and watch the current of people go past. The line stops at a terminus two streets from my house, and the condition of the road there is terrible. My father uses the same word for the season, the school and the length of a loan. He says a word is only a tool, and a tool should be used more than once.","zh":"学期还有三周就结束了。在这门学科里，谓语承载了大部分意思，一个用错的词就能改变整句。阅读量不大，趣味性却不少。每天早上我站在公交总站看人流经过。这条线路的终点站离我家两条街，而那里路况糟透了。"},"wild":{"tw":[["wilderness",4],["crazy",0],["barren",3],["tame",1],["fish",6],["waste",0],["bird",6],["furious",0]],"en":"The garden has gone wild again. Beyond the fence there is a piece of wilderness where no bird has nested for years and the ground is barren. My neighbour is furious about the waste of good land, and he says only a crazy man would leave it like that. His own cat is tame and fat. I go there to fish in the small stream and to be alone for an hour. In spring the stream is full of small fish and the birds come back to the fence. Nobody in the village has walked to the far end of it for years.","zh":"园子又野了。栅栏那边有一片荒地，多年没有鸟在这里筑巢，土地贫瘠。我邻居对这么好的一块地被浪费感到愤怒，他说只有疯子才会让它这样。他自己那只猫又温顺又肥。我去那里的小溪里钓鱼，独自待上一个小时。"},"act":{"tw":[["begin",3],["serve",2],["refrain",1],["move",0],["deal",3],["event",2],["order",6],["play",0]],"en":"The act begins at seven. First they serve the soup, then the play starts, and nobody may move from their seat. I have to deal with the last table and give the order to the kitchen before the second act. Please refrain from talking during the music. The whole event lasts two hours, and by the end my feet are dead. The same thing happens every Friday, and I still enjoy it. The young woman who plays the mother has never acted before, and she is very good. After the last curtain we wash the glasses and count the money.","zh":"这幕戏七点开始。先上汤，然后戏才开演，谁都不许离开座位。我得收拾最后一张桌子，并在第二幕之前把点单送进厨房。音乐响起时请勿交谈。整个活动持续两小时，结束时我的脚都站麻了。每周五都是这样，而我依然挺喜欢。"},"add":{"tw":[["bring",0],["subtract",1],["combine",6],["total",0],["include",3],["count",2],["extra",6],["contribute",0]],"en":"Please add these two figures and bring me the total. You may not subtract anything, and you must include the extra charge for delivery. If you combine the two lists, the count will be wrong by one. Everyone in the office had to contribute a little. I checked it twice before I took it in, and the answer looked simple to everybody. The figures come from two different books, and each one has its own way of counting. If the total is not the same in both, we start again from the beginning.","zh":"请把这两个数字加起来，把总数拿来给我。不许减掉任何一项，还必须把额外的运费算进去。如果把两张清单合并，计数就会差一个。办公室里每个人都得出一点力。我交上去之前核了两遍，而在所有人看来答案都显而易见。"},"agree":{"tw":[["check",0],["accept",2],["disagree",1],["consider",6],["fit",0],["meet",3],["suit",2],["negotiate",6]],"en":"I agree with you about the price, but I cannot accept the date. We can meet on Thursday and negotiate the rest. Let me check the small room first; if the table does not fit, the whole plan is no good. Consider the other offer before you decide. My brother disagrees with me and says the later date would suit him much better. He wants the later date because his son will be home from the army by then. That is a good reason, and I have no good reason of my own.","zh":"价钱上我同意你，但日期我不能接受。我们周四见面，其余的事再谈。先让我看看那间小屋；桌子放不下的话，整个计划就不行。做决定前你也考虑一下另一个报价。我哥哥不同意我，他说晚一点那个日期对他合适得多。"},"allow":{"tw":[["admit",3],["accept",2],["deny",1],["require",6],["trust",3],["assign",2],["enable",6],["grant",0]],"en":"They do not allow dogs in the shop. The sign says they cannot admit animals, and they deny that it has anything to do with the owner. Anyone who wants to bring one must accept the rule. The job will require an hour of training, and the manager will assign somebody to help you. This small key will enable you to open the back door. I trust they will grant us one more week. The shop next door allows them, and half the street goes there instead. The owner says he will not change his mind, and I believe him.","zh":"他们不许带狗进店。牌子上说不能接纳动物，他们否认这与主人有关。想带狗来的人必须接受这条规矩。这份活需要一小时培训，经理会指派一个人帮你。这把小钥匙能让你打开后门。我相信他们会再宽限我们一周。"},"answer":{"tw":[["reply",2],["field",3],["meet",2],["question",1],["serve",3],["counter",3],["state",2],["result",0]],"en":"I wrote my answer and put it on the counter. There was no reply for a week, and then a short letter came. The state of the field is the real question here: nobody can meet in a wet meadow, and the result would be a mess. I asked again at the second window, and the woman there could not serve me either. So I went home and waited for the third letter. In the third week I met the owner himself at the door of the office. He answered every question except the one I had actually asked.","zh":"我把答案写好放在柜台上。一周都没有回音，然后来了一封短信。这里的真正问题是场地状况：没人能在湿草地里集会，结果只会一团糟。我又到第二个窗口去问，那里的女士也帮不了我。于是我回家等第三封信。"},"bottom":{"tw":[["bed",0],["base",3],["hit",2],["side",2],["spot",6],["behind",0],["foot",3],["land",2],["plate",6]],"en":"At the bottom of the garden there is a bed of stones. The base of the old wall is under it, and on the far side you can see a plate of iron fixed into the ground. We used to hit it with a stick when we were children. The spot behind the tree is where my dog liked to sleep. From there you can put your foot on the land beyond the fence. In summer the whole garden smells of wet stone, and the bed under the wall is the coolest place in it.","zh":"园子最底下有一片石头地。那堵旧墙的基座就在下面，靠外的一侧能看到一块嵌进地里的铁板。我们小时候常拿棍子敲它。树后那一处是我家狗爱睡的地方。从那儿你可以把脚伸到栅栏外的土地上去。"},"break":{"tw":[["blow",3],["change",2],["repair",1],["check",0],["chip",3],["dance",2],["die",0],["back",6]],"en":"Take a break at four; you look tired. A single blow from that hammer can chip the stone, and the break in the wall will only get worse. Nobody can repair it in one day, and a small change here will not help. Check the back of the house first, where the wind comes in. The old tree will die this year. Come and dance with me instead; the wall has waited thirty years. The crack runs from the window down to the floor, and in winter it lets the cold air in.","zh":"四点歇一下吧，你看上去累了。那把锤子敲一下就能把石头崩出缺口，而墙上的裂口只会越来越大。一天之内谁也修不好，在这里做点小改动也没用。先去查看房子背面，风是从那儿灌进来的。那棵老树今年会死。不如过来跟我跳舞吧，那堵墙等了三十年了。"},"change":{"tw":[["alter",0],["break",3],["dress",2],["stay",1],["exchange",0],["cut",3],["travel",2],["reason",6],["shift",0]],"en":"You cannot change this without asking. Nothing can alter the size of the door, and if you cut the frame you will break the glass. There is a good reason for the rule: the shift of the wind in winter is strong enough to travel through any small gap. I had to dress in two coats and stay inside. In the future we will exchange the old panes for new ones. Anything you alter in this room has to be written in the book by the door. The book has been there for a hundred years and the handwriting is very small.","zh":"不打招呼你不能改动这里。门的尺寸无法更改，要是削了框子就会打碎玻璃。这条规定有它的道理：冬天风向一变，风大得能从任何小缝里钻进来。我不得不穿上两件外套待在屋里。以后我们会把旧玻璃换成新的。"},"clean":{"tw":[["clear",0],["wash",3],["change",2],["dirty",1],["enough",6],["fair",5],["brush",3],["remove",2],["water",6],["fresh",0]],"en":"Keep the room clean: wash the floor, brush the table and remove every plate before you leave. The water in the bucket must be clear, not fresh, and the cloth has to be clean enough to use twice. If the sheets are dirty, change them. It is not fair to leave that work to the next person. I have done it for eleven years, and the room has never once been dirty on my shift. When the shift ends I put the brushes back in the cupboard and lock it. The next person will find everything exactly where it belongs.","zh":"把屋子保持干净：走之前擦地、刷桌、把所有盘子收走。桶里的水要清，不必是新打的；抹布得干净到还能再用一次。床单脏了就换。把活儿留给下一个人是不公平的。我干了十一年，我班上这屋子从没脏过。"},"comfort":{"tw":[["ease",0],["calm",3],["aid",2],["discomfort",1],["sense",6],["console",0],["relief",3],["condition",2]],"en":"The old chair gives me more comfort than the new one. It has a calm shape and a soft cushion, and when my back is bad it is a real aid. The discomfort in my knees goes away within a minute of sitting down. My only sense of relief in the evening comes from that chair. My sister tries to console me by saying it is an ordinary chair, but she does not have to sit in it all day. For ease of mind I have written its condition on a card and hung the card on the back of the chair.","zh":"那把旧椅子比新的更让我舒服。它形制沉静、坐垫柔软，我背痛的时候它真帮得上忙。一坐下不到一分钟，膝盖的不适就消失了。晚上我唯一的放松感就来自那把椅子。我妹妹想安慰我，说那只是把普通的椅子，可她不用整天坐在上面。"},"continue":{"tw":[["cover",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["discontinue",1],["bring",6],["stay",0],["cross",3],["talk",2],["extend",0],["move",6]],"en":"We will continue the work tomorrow. Nobody can carry on like this: two of the men have gone home and the rain shows no sign of stopping. Every act of repair here begins in the rain. If they discontinue the service, we will have to cover the roof ourselves and stay until it is done. I cannot talk about it any longer. Let us cross the yard, move the boxes inside, and then we will extend the plan by a week. Somebody has to bring the tarpaulin before the night shift starts.","zh":"明天我们继续干。没人能这样撑下去：两个人已经回家了，雨也没有要停的样子。这里每一次修理都是在雨里开的头。要是他们停掉这项服务，我们就得自己盖屋顶，一直干完为止。我不能再聊这个了。我们穿过院子，把箱子搬进屋，然后把这个计划延长一周。"},"air":{"tw":[["aerial",4],["line",0],["breath",3],["dry",2],["light",6],["aerate",4],["send",0],["note",3],["gas",2],["jet",6],["atmosphere",0]],"en":"The small radio station sits on a hill where the air is dry and clear. Every morning the engineer opens the windows to aerate the room before the first show. She sends the signal along one line to a tall aerial on the roof, and from there it travels by jet to towns far away. The music she plays has a simple air, a tune you can hum note by note. The light from her desk lamp is the only other thing in the room. She takes a deep breath, waits for the gas heater to warm the air, and thinks about the wide atmosphere outside.","zh":"那座小电台坐落在山丘上，那儿的空气又干又清。每天早上，工程师都要打开窗户，让直播间的空气流通一下，然后才开始第一档节目。她把信号顺着一条线路送到屋顶那根高高的天线上，再从那里传往很远的小镇。她放的音乐调子很简单，是可以一个音符一个音符哼出来的。书桌台灯的光是屋里唯一另外的亮处。她深吸一口气，等着煤气取暖器把空气烘暖，心里想着外面那一片广阔的天地。"},"live":{"tw":[["liver",4],["experience",2],["board",3],["dead",1],["except",6],["hot",0],["camp",3],["alone",6],["last",0]],"en":"My uncle has lived in a camp near the river for ten years, mostly alone. He is not dead, though some of the men he worked with are. He says the only thing that makes a long stay bearable is experience: you learn which food is safe and which water is hot enough to drink. Except for the winter, he is out on the board path every morning. Doctors once told him his liver was weak, so he eats little meat and walks a lot. He wants to live in a real house last of all, but not yet.","zh":"我叔叔在河边的一个营地里住了十年，大多时候是一个人。他没死，虽然跟他一起干过活的人里有些已经不在了。他说，能让这种长住熬得下去的只有经验：你得知道哪些东西能吃，哪里的水烧热了才能喝。除了冬天，他每天早上都出门，走那条木板路。医生曾说他肝不好，所以他少吃肉、多走路。他说到最后还是想住进一间真正的房子，但不是现在。"},"sky":{"tw":[["celestial",4],["flip",0],["lag",3],["horizon",6],["fling",2],["pitch",0],["submarine",3],["bright",6],["toss",0]],"en":"On the last night of the trip we lay on the deck and watched the sky. It was bright, with no cloud at all, and a few celestial bodies moved slowly above the horizon. My brother began to toss a coin and flip it, trying to catch it in the dark. Each pitch of the boat made him lag behind the beat of the waves, and once the coin went over the side. A submarine lamp far off threw a pale line on the water. He gave a little fling of his arm and laughed. We stayed out until the sky turned grey.","zh":"旅途的最后一晚，我们躺在甲上看天。天很亮，一丝云也没有，几颗星星慢慢地移过地平线。我弟弟开始抛硬币、翻着玩，想在黑里接住它。船每颠一下，他就比浪的节拍慢半拍，有一次硬币掉进了海里。远处一盏潜水艇的灯在水面上投下一道淡淡的白线。他手臂一甩，笑了。我们在外面待到天色发灰。"},"cry":{"tw":[["call",0],["noise",3],["change",2],["laugh",1],["remember",6],["shout",0],["tear",3],["express",2],["wonder",6],["scream",3]],"en":"When the baby began to cry, my sister did not shout or scream. She picked him up and made a low sound, a kind of call that he seemed to remember from another night. The noise in the flat was terrible, so she took him to the window for a change of air. He would laugh, then cry again, and a single tear ran down his cheek. I wonder how a small child can express so much with one sound. She said that all mothers learn it, and that she would remember it for the rest of her life.","zh":"孩子一哭，我姐姐既没有喊也没有尖叫。她把他抱起来，发出一个很低的声音，像是某种呼唤，他好像记得这是从别的夜里听过的。屋里的噪声糟透了，她抱他到窗边换换空气。他笑一下，又哭起来，一滴眼泪顺着脸颊往下流。我奇怪一个这么小的孩子怎么能用一声哭表达这么多。她说当妈的都会这一手，她一辈子都会记得。"},"empty":{"tw":[["abandon",0],["clear",3],["change",2],["fill",1],["inside",6],["discharge",0],["bleed",3],["leave",2],["room",6],["hollow",0]],"en":"The old factory was empty when we got there. Someone had left the gate open, and a clear wind blew through a broken window. We had come to change the locks and fill the holes in the floor. Inside, a great hollow tank stood against the wall where the water used to be stored. They had to discharge the last of it through a pipe, and a thin stream continued to bleed onto the concrete for an hour. I could not abandon the place; it was the room where my father worked. We would leave it standing, at least for one more year.","zh":"我们到的时候，那家老厂是空的。有人把大门敞着，一股清亮的风从破窗里穿过去。我们来是为了换锁，再把地板上的洞补上。屋里靠墙立着一个巨大的空罐子，从前就是在那儿储水的。剩下的水得从一根管子里排出去，细细的一股流在水泥地上淌了一个小时。我没法把这儿丢下不要；这是我父亲当年干活的车间。我们决定先让它立着，至少再留一年。"},"express":{"tw":[["carry",0],["drop",3],["mail",2],["local",1],["message",6],["state",0],["raise",3],["communicate",2],["service",6],["convey",2]],"en":"The local post office will not carry a parcel that is too heavy, so I had to express it instead. The clerk asked me to state the value and then to raise the box onto the scale. She said the mail service would get the message to my brother by Friday. I tried to convey how urgent it was, and she promised to drop it in the first van out. The old way of sending letters could not communicate such speed. I paid, took the receipt, and left feeling that the whole thing had gone well.","zh":"本地的邮局不收太重的包裹，所以我只好走快递。柜台的人让我报一下价值，再把箱子抬到秤上。她说邮件服务周五之前能把消息送到我哥哥手上。我想让她明白这事有多急，她答应把这箱子塞进第一班发走的车里。从前寄信的老法子根本传达不了这么快的速度。我付了钱，拿了收据，走的时候觉得整件事办得挺顺。"},"fall":{"tw":[["autumn",0],["break",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["end",6],["drop",3],["rain",3],["die",2],["since",6],["hang",0]],"en":"Since the end of summer, the leaves have begun to fall. Each autumn I watch them drop from the tall trees behind the house, and they hang in the wet air before they reach the ground. The change comes quickly here: one week it is warm, the next the rain will not stop. Prices rise, the shops break their old rules and close early, and a few small birds die in the cold. My mother says this is the finest time of year, when the garden falls quiet. It is only October, and already the wood box by the door is full.","zh":"入夏以来，叶子就开始落了。每年秋天我都看着它们从屋后那些大树上掉下来，落地之前先悬在潮湿的空气里。这里变天变得快：这一周还暖着，下一周雨就下个不停。物价往上涨，店家打破了老规矩提前关门，几只小鸟冻死了。我妈说这是一年里最好的时节，园子静下来的时候。才十月，门边那只木箱子已经装满了。"},"feed":{"tw":[["course",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["starve",1],["consume",6],["eat",0],["dine",3],["provide",2],["grow",6],["run",0]],"en":"My aunt runs a small farm and has to feed forty animals before she can feed herself. Of course the cost has gone up, and she refuses to waste a single sack of grain. Each morning she will move the sheep to a new field, then provide water for the cows and let the young ones run about. In winter there is little to eat, and the weakest may starve if the hay does not last. At night she will dine alone in the kitchen, proud that the whole place can grow and consume and still pay for itself.","zh":"我姑姑经营一个小农场，得先把四十头牲口喂饱，才轮到自己吃饭。成本当然涨了，她一袋粮食都不肯糟蹋。每天早上她把羊赶到新的一片地里，然后给牛添水，让小牛四处跑。冬天没什么可吃的，草料要是撑不到开春，最弱的那几头就可能饿死。晚上她一个人在厨房吃饭，很得意这块地方能种能养、还能自己养自己。"},"fill":{"tw":[["meet",0],["answer",3],["change",2],["empty",1],["extra",6],["satisfy",0],["close",3],["enough",2],["room",6],["fulfil",0]],"en":"We had to fill the hall before eight o'clock, but the room was still half empty when the band began. An extra row of chairs helped, and by the time the door had to close there was enough space for everyone. The manager said we could not satisfy a crowd like that with a small show, so he had to change the programme and answer a few angry phone calls. In the end we did meet the promise and fulfil the plan. I sat at the back and watched the seats fill one by one.","zh":"我们得在八点前把礼堂填满，可乐队开场时屋子还空着一半。加了一排椅子才管用，等到不得不关门的时候，位子已经够所有人坐了。经理说这种规模的观众，小节目是满足不了的，于是他改了节目单，还接了几个气冲冲的电话。最后我们总算兑现了承诺，把计划做成了。我坐在最后一排，看着座位一个个被填满。"},"find":{"tw":[["chance",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["lose",1],["how",6],["discover",0],["count",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["feel",3]],"en":"I had to find the key before my father came home, and I was not sure how to do it. There was a chance he had left it in the car, so I went out to look. I had to act quickly, count the minutes while I searched, and feel along every shelf. I did not want to lose my nerve or let the light change before I was finished. Then I began to discover small things: a torn ticket, a note, and at last the key itself. I managed to catch the door just as he turned into the road.","zh":"我必须在爸爸回家之前找到钥匙，可我不确定该怎么办。有可能他把它落在车里了，于是我就出去找。我得赶紧动手，一边找一边数着分钟，把每个架子都摸一遍。我不想在这期间慌了神，也不想等天光变了还没找完。后来我开始发现一些小东西：一张撕破的票、一张纸条，最后就是钥匙本身。他拐进这条路的时候，我刚好把门接住。"},"finish":{"tw":[["close",3],["break",3],["act",2],["start",1],["straight",6],["complete",0],["draw",3],["coat",2],["round",6],["end",3]],"en":"The painter said he would finish the room in three days, but the start was slow. He had to draw the shape of each window first, then work in a straight line down the wall. We would break for tea at eleven and close the door so the dust did not reach the hall. The first coat took a whole day; the second was quicker. At the end of the round he asked me to act as judge and look for any thin patch. It was complete by Friday, and the whole job turned out better than I had hoped.","zh":"油漆工说三天就能把这间屋子刷完，可开头很慢。他得先把每扇窗的形状描出来，再顺着墙面一笔直着往下刷。十一点我们会停下来喝茶，把门关上，免得灰飘到走廊里。第一遍漆刷了一整天，第二遍就快多了。这一轮收尾的时候，他让我当裁判，去找有没有刷薄的地方。到周五就全完工了，整件活儿比我想的还好。"},"follow":{"tw":[["watch",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["precede",1],["change",6],["observe",0],["chase",3],["check",2],["see",6],["trace",0]],"en":"A good guide will follow the old path and never act on guesswork. He will watch the sky, observe where the birds go, and check the marks on the trees. The men who precede him leave signs, and he can trace every one of them. If the wind should change, he must carry on without complaint and chase the last of the light. I have seen him do it a hundred times. You follow because you trust him, not because you can see the way yourself. The rest of us simply walk behind and try not to lose him.","zh":"好向导会跟着那条老路走，绝不凭猜行事。他会看天，观察鸟往哪儿飞，检查树上的记号。走在他前面的人留下标记，他能把每一个都追踪出来。风要是变了向，他也得一声不吭地往前走，追着最后一点天光。我见他这么干过一百回。你跟着他，是因为信得过他，不是因为你自个儿看得清路。我们这些剩下的人只管在后面走，尽量别跟丢。"},"foot":{"tw":[["base",0],["bed",3],["add",2],["head",1],["hole",6],["pick",0],["paw",3],["bottom",2],["inside",6],["infantry",0]],"en":"There was a hole in my boot, and by the end of the walk my foot was wet. The base of the hill is soft, so each step sank a little, and I had to pick my way between the stones. My dog ran ahead on a heavy paw, then stopped and put his head down at the bottom of a wall. Inside the old shed we found a bed of dry grass and a line of marks that looked like an army. My father said the infantry had camped there long ago, before the road was built. He added that his own feet still hurt from that winter.","zh":"我靴子上有个洞，走到最后脚全湿了。山脚下土很松，每一步都往下陷一点，我只得在石头之间挑着路走。我的狗用一只厚爪子跑在前面，忽然停下来，把头低在一堵墙脚下。在那间旧棚子里，我们找到一片干草铺的窝，还有一排看着像脚印的痕迹。我爸说很久以前、路还没修的时候，步兵在这儿扎过营。他又说他的脚到现在还记得那个冬天。"},"free":{"tw":[["rid",0],["clear",5],["issue",2],["confine",1],["without",6],["innocent",0],["cut",3],["pass",2],["allow",6],["loose",5]],"en":"The court set him free after nine months. He had been confined to a small cell without a window, and no one would allow him to see the papers in his own case. The judge said he was innocent, that the police had no right to cut him off from his family, and that the whole issue was a mistake. He walked out, let his shoulders go loose, and took a clear breath of morning air. He wanted only to be rid of the past and to pass through the gate like any other man.","zh":"九个月后，法庭把他放了。他先前被关在一间没有窗的小牢房里，谁也不让他看自己案子的卷宗。法官说他是无罪的，警方没有权利把他和家人隔开，说整件事就是个错误。他走出来，把肩膀松开，清清爽爽地吸了一口早晨的空气。他只想把过去甩掉，像个普通人一样从大门走出去。"},"freeze":{"tw":[["block",0],["ice",3],["act",2],["boil",1],["resume",6],["frost",3],["fixate",3],["change",2],["unless",6],["halt",0]],"en":"Unless the pipes are wrapped, the water in them will freeze on the first cold night. Last year the ice blocked the whole line and the heating had to halt for two days. My neighbour began to fixate on the weather report, watching for frost and for any change in the wind. We agreed to act together: he would boil water for the old man next door while I went to get salt. In the morning the thaw came, and the traffic could resume along the main road. For a week nothing moved, and we counted the days by the marks on the kitchen wall.","zh":"管子要是不包上，里头的水在第一个寒夜就会冻住。去年冰把整条管线堵死了，暖气不得不停了整整两天。我邻居开始盯着天气预报不放，一心等霜冻、等风向有什么变化。我们说好一起动手：他去给隔壁老人烧水，我去弄盐。早上化冻了，大路上的车又能走了。那一个星期什么也动不了，我们就在厨房墙上划道子数日子。"},"front":{"tw":[["face",3],["nose",3],["lie",2],["back",1],["inside",6],["look",0],["bow",3],["line",2],["behind",6],["breast",0]],"en":"The old house stands at the front of a narrow street, with a small garden behind it. Its face is grey, and the paint on the nose of each window has worn away. Inside, a long line of photographs hangs on the wall, and the ones at the back are almost white. My grandmother would look at them and bow her head a little. She said the house must not lie empty, that a family should live at its breast, close to the road, where everyone can see who comes and goes.","zh":"那栋老房子立在一条窄街的最前头，后面有个小园子。它的门面是灰的，每扇窗子凸出来的那块漆都磨掉了。屋里墙上挂着一长排照片，靠里的那些几乎白得看不清了。我奶奶会看着它们，微微低下头。她说这房子不能空着躺在那儿，一家人该住在它的胸口上，紧挨着大路，好让谁都看得见谁进谁出。"},"good":{"tw":[["dear",0],["basic",3],["advantage",2],["bad",1],["sure",6],["full",0],["better",3],["quality",2],["think",6],["near",0]],"en":"My grandfather always said that a good name is worth more than money. He kept the shop near the bridge for forty years and never once sold anything of poor quality. Of course it was hard to make a living, but he thought the basic advantage of the work was simple: people trusted him, and trust is a dear thing. When trade turned bad he did not complain. He was sure that if he stayed full of patience things would get better, and in the end they did. That, he said, was the whole of the matter.","zh":"我爷爷总说，好名声比钱值钱。他在桥边开那家铺子开了四十年，一回也没卖过差东西。谋生当然不容易，但他觉得这活儿最基本的好处很简单：人家信得过他，而信得过是很金贵的东西。生意变差的时候他也不抱怨。他认定只要耐着性子熬着，日子总会好起来，后来果然就好了。他说，事情的全部就是这个。"},"ground":{"tw":[["base",0],["build",3],["hit",2],["figure",1],["fire",6],["earth",3],["floor",3],["paint",2],["inside",6],["land",2]],"en":"The workers had to clear the ground before they could build anything. They hit a thick layer of clay at the base of the slope, and the figure on their plan had to be changed. Inside the fence the floor of the old shed was still there, with a door of green paint and the marks of an old fire on the wall. The land belonged to a family who had farmed it for a hundred years. Now a line of lorries carries away the earth and nothing will grow on that ground for a long time.","zh":"工人们得先把地清出来才能动工盖东西。他们在坡底下一头撞上厚厚一层黏土，图纸上的数字只得改了。围墙里面，那间旧棚子的地面还在，还有一扇刷绿漆的门和墙上的一个壁炉。这块地属于一家人，他们种了一百年。现在一队卡车把土一车车运走，那片地上很久都不会再长出什么来了。"},"hit":{"tw":[["reach",0],["bottom",3],["move",2],["miss",1],["run",6],["shoot",0],["cut",3],["touch",2],["double",6],["strike",0]],"en":"The batsman waited, watched the ball, and then hit it hard. The crowd rose as it began to reach the far side of the field, and the men on the boundary had to run. He did not miss once that afternoon, and twice he made the ball touch the top of the wall for a double. When the light began to go, the captain told him to cut the risk and stop trying to shoot at everything. He moved down the pitch slowly, took one last strike, and the ball rolled to the bottom of the bank.","zh":"击球手等着，盯着球，然后狠狠一击。球开始飞向场地那头，看台上的人都站起来了，边界上的几个球员只得跑起来。那天下午他一次也没落空，还有两回让球碰到墙顶，跑成两分。天光渐暗时，队长叫他别再冒风险，不要见什么都打。他慢慢地走下球道，最后一击，球滚到了坡底。"},"issue":{"tw":[["cut",0],["change",3],["store",2],["recall",1],["question",6],["matter",0],["check",3],["write",2],["whether",6],["return",0]],"en":"The manager had to recall a whole line of tins and issue a notice to every store in the district. The question was whether the fault came from the factory or from the long journey in the heat. He asked me to check the records and write a short report on the matter. There had been a change in the way the lids were cut, and nobody could say when it started. We had to return three hundred boxes to the plant. It was a small issue, but it cost us a month.","zh":"经理不得不召回一整批罐头，并向区里每家商店发一份通知。问题在于毛病出在工厂，还是出在炎热天气里那趟长途运输。他让我去核一下记录，就这件事写一份简短的报告。罐盖的裁切方式有过一次改动，谁也说不清是从什么时候开始的。我们得把三百箱货退回厂里。事情本身不大，却耗了我们一个月。"},"last":{"tw":[["close",0],["run",3],["measure",2],["first",1],["ago",6],["end",2],["wear",3],["rank",2],["since",6],["final",0]],"en":"My last summer at the school began long ago in the first week of June and ended in the middle of August. I had to run a mile every morning, and the coach would measure the time and write it on the board. Since the oldest boys always took the top rank, I never came close to them. By the final week my shoes had begun to wear through at the toe. On the last day the whole class stood in a line at the end of the field, and the headmaster said a few words that I have carried with me for a long time.","zh":"我在学校过的最后一个夏天，是从六月的第一周开始，到八月中结束的。每天早上我都得跑一英里，教练会量时间，再写在校牌上。因为最高名次总被年纪最大的那几个占着，我从来没能靠近他们。到了最后一周，我的鞋脚尖已经开始磨穿了。最后一天，全班在场地尽头站成一排，校长讲了几句话，那些话我一直记到今天。"},"law":{"tw":[["lawyer",4],["police",0],["force",2],["justice",6],["legal",4],["philosophy",2],["statute",6]],"en":"My cousin trained as a lawyer and now works for a small firm that takes cases the police will not touch. He says the law is not the same thing as justice, and that any statute can be read in two ways. The force of an old rule may last for a century after the reason for it is gone. At night he reads a little philosophy, because the questions he meets in court are older than any legal book. He tells me that most of what people call justice is really just care taken with details.","zh":"我表哥学的是法律，现在在一家小事务所做事，接的都是警方不愿沾的案子。他说法律和公正不是一回事，任何一条成文法都能有两种读法。一条旧规矩的效力，可能在它的道理早就没了之后还要撑上一百年。夜里他会读一点哲学，因为他在法庭上遇到的那些问题，比任何法学书都古老。他跟我说，人们嘴里的公正，多半不过是对细节的一点点用心。"},"leave":{"tw":[["allow",0],["pass",3],["change",2],["arrive",1],["stay",6],["forget",0],["remember",3],["lose",2],["return",6],["lead",3]],"en":"We had to leave the hotel before six, and the manager would not allow us to stay a minute longer. The train was due to arrive at half past, so we had to pass through the empty streets with our bags. My mother kept checking that she was not forgetting anything, and then, of course, she would remember something else. I was afraid we should lose the connection at the next station. But the change was easy, and by noon we had returned to the town that had led us out thirty years before.","zh":"我们六点前就得离开旅馆，经理一分钟都不肯让我们多留。火车半点到，所以我们只好拎着箱子穿过空荡荡的街道。我妈一遍遍检查自己有没有忘东西，然后当然又想起来了别的。我担心我们在下一站会误了换乘。可换车很顺利，中午的时候，我们已经回到了三十年前带我们离开的那座小镇。"},"level":{"tw":[["charge",0],["high",3],["state",2],["raise",1],["current",6],["flat",0],["low",3],["talk",2],["below",6],["floor",3]],"en":"The engineer stood on the floor of the hall and checked the level of the water in the tank. It was still low, only a metre below the mark, so he had to raise the pipe and let the current run for an hour. He did not want to charge the whole system again, because the pressure was already high. His talk with the manager had been short and flat: either the state of the pumps improved, or the building would have to close for a week. In the end he found a simple answer and wrote it down on the wall.","zh":"工程师站在大厅的地面上，查看水箱里的水位。水还很低，离刻线只差一米，所以他得把管子抬高，让水流上一个小时。他不想再给整个系统充一次压，因为压力本来就高。他跟经理那番谈话又短又平淡：要么水泵的状况好转，要么这栋楼就得关一个星期。最后他想出个简单的办法，把它写在了墙上。"},"lie":{"tw":[["rest",0],["back",3],["position",2],["sit",1],["hide",6],["consist",0],["charge",3],["exist",2],["else",6],["dwell",0]],"en":"The old dog likes to lie in the same place every evening, at the back of the kitchen where nobody else goes. His position never changes; he will rest there for hours and only sit up when he hears a car. I asked the vet whether any trouble might hide behind such quiet habits, and she said that a dog's health can consist of very little: food, warmth, and a good place to sleep. She told me not to charge him with anything more, and to let him dwell in his own corner as long as he exists.","zh":"那条老狗每天傍晚都要躺在一个固定的地方，就是厨房里头谁也去不到的角落。它的位置从不改变；它能在那里歇上好几个钟头，只有听见车声才坐起来。我问兽医，这么安静的习性背后会不会藏着什么毛病。她说狗的健康其实可以由很少的东西组成：吃食、暖和，再加一个睡觉的好地方。她叫我别再给它加什么负担，让它就在自己的角落里待着，活一天算一天。"},"like":{"tw":[["care",0],["love",3],["see",2],["dislike",1],["look",6],["same",5],["please",3],["desire",2],["well",6],["wish",0]],"en":"My sister and I look exactly the same, and we like the same things. But she does not care for cold mornings, and I dislike them even more. As you wish, she said one day, but I should love a walk by the river. I could see she was not well, so I did not please her. Her one desire was a hot drink and a long rest. I looked at her face and thought how much alike we were, and how little it mattered. We were like two cups thrown by the same hand, and neither of us could be happy alone.","zh":"我和姐姐长得一模一样，喜欢的东西也一样。可她受不了冷天早晨，我比她更讨厌。有一天她说：随你吧，不过我倒是很想沿河走一走。我看得出她身子不舒服，就没顺着她。她唯一的念头是一杯热饮和好好歇一会儿。我看着她那张脸，心想我们俩多像啊，而这又多么不重要。我们像同一双手捏出来的两只杯子，谁单独一个都不会快活。"},"love":{"tw":[["bed",0],["romance",3],["like",2],["hate",1],["dream",6],["dear",0],["worship",3],["object",2],["mind",6],["bang",0]],"en":"My grandmother says she did not fall in love with my grandfather at first sight; she simply liked him and went on liking him. There was no romance in the little flat where they began, only one bed and a window over the yard. I hate to say it, she told me, but after fifty years the dear old man is still the first object in my mind. She keeps his picture by her bed and worships the ground he walks on. She has a dream that they will meet again. Then she banged the kettle down and laughed at herself.","zh":"我奶奶说，她对我爷爷不是一见钟情；她只是一开始喜欢他，然后就一直喜欢下去。他们起头的那间小公寓里没什么浪漫，只有一张床和一扇朝院子的窗。她跟我说：我不愿意这么说，可过了五十年，这个老头子还是我心里头头一件放着的事。她把他照片摆在床边，把他走过的地都当圣地。她还做着再见到他的梦。说完她把水壶往下一磕，自己笑了。"},"man":{"tw":[["human",0],["black",3],["island",2],["woman",1],["boy",6],["piece",0],["white",3],["work",2],["old",6],["world",3]],"en":"The old man lived alone on the island for eleven years after his wife died. He was the only human being there, and for a long time he did not see a woman or a boy. His house was one long piece of white stone above the black rocks, and he kept it in good work by mending the roof every spring. When people asked how he could bear it, he said the world was large enough for one man if he watched it closely. Now he is gone, and only the garden shows where he lived.","zh":"妻子去世后，那个老人在岛上独自住了十一年。整座岛上只有他一个人，很长一段时间里，他见不到一个女人，也见不到一个男孩。他的房子是黑礁石上头一块长长的白石头，每年春天他修一次屋顶，把它收拾得挺像样。有人问他怎么熬得住，他说，一个人只要看得够仔细，这世界对他就够大了。现在他不在了，只有那片园子还显示他曾经住过。"},"manage":{"tw":[["care",0],["build",3],["act",2],["fail",1],["help",6],["deal",0],["meet",3],["control",2],["need",6],["handle",0]],"en":"She has to manage a small shop and a family at the same time, and she does it well. She will build the week's plan on Sunday, deal with the suppliers on Monday, and meet her customers every day. If she should fail at anything, she does not need anyone to tell her. She can handle a difficult customer better than most people I know, and she is never rude. The one thing she cannot control is her own tiredness. I act as if I were fine, she says, and then I take care of myself on Sunday. Her sister comes in to help on Saturdays.","zh":"她既要管一家小店，又要管家，两头都顾得很好。她星期天把一周的打算排出来，星期一跟供货的人打交道，每天还要见客人。要是哪件事没办成，她不用别人说。难缠的客人，她应付得比我认识的多数人都好，而且从不失礼。唯一她管不住的就是自己的累。她说：我就装作没事，然后星期天再照顾自己。星期六她妹妹会过来搭把手。"},"miss":{"tw":[["drop",0],["cut",3],["woman",2],["hit",1],["play",6],["lose",0],["forget",3],["avoid",2],["title",6],["escape",0]],"en":"The woman in the next seat told me not to miss the first ten minutes of the play. She had a title in her hand and kept checking it. If you drop in late, she said, you lose the whole point. I did not want to hit anyone with my bag, so I cut along the wall and sat down quickly. I tried to avoid the man with the loud voice, but I could not forget how close I had come to being late. That day I learned to leave the house early and never miss a train again. There is no escape from that lesson once it is learned.","zh":"邻座那位女士叫我千万别错过这出戏开头那十分钟。她手里捏着节目单，一遍遍看。她说：你要是迟到了再进去，整出戏的意思就丢了。我不想用包撞到人，就贴着墙边挤过去，赶紧坐下。我想躲开那个嗓门大的男人，可忘不掉自己差一点就迟到。那天我算是学乖了：出门要早，再也不能误车。这教训一旦学到手，就再也躲不开了。"},"open":{"tw":[["clear",0],["establish",3],["move",2],["close",1],["next",6],["subject",0],["gap",3],["start",2],["round",6],["loose",0]],"en":"The committee met in an open room on the second floor, with a clear view of the yard. Before the start of business they had to establish who would speak first, then move the tables into a loose round so everyone could see the others. There was a gap at the door, which they left open for air. Half the subject that day was the next budget, but by six o'clock they had still not voted to close the meeting. In the end they agreed to carry the matter over to the following week, and the room emptied in a minute.","zh":"委员会在二楼一间敞亮的屋子里开会，从那儿能把院子看得清清楚楚。开会之前，他们得先定下谁第一个发言，然后把桌子摆成一个松松的圈，好让每个人都看得见别人。门那儿有条缝，他们就让它敞着透气。那天的议题有一半是下一年的预算，可到六点他们还没表决要不要散会。最后他们说好把这事推到下个星期，屋子里一分钟就走空了。"},"question":{"tw":[["doubt",0],["problem",3],["ask",2],["answer",1],["whether",6],["head",0],["pump",3],["subject",2],["reason",6],["wonder",3]],"en":"The teacher would ask one question and then wait, with her head a little to one side. There was no doubt in her mind that a good problem is worth more than a quick answer. I wonder, she would say, whether any of you can tell me the reason for this. Then she would pump the water out of an old pipe to show us what she meant. The subject of the lesson was pressure, but what she really taught us was to sit with a question instead of reaching for the first thing that came.","zh":"老师会先提一个问题，然后等着，头微微偏到一边。她心里从不怀疑：一个好问题比一个快答案值钱。她会说：我倒想知道，你们谁说得清这里头的道理。接着她会用一根旧管子把水抽出来，让我们看看她是什么意思。那节课的主题是压力，可她真正教我们的是：守着一个问题待着，别急着去抓头一个冒出来的东西。"},"quiet":{"tw":[["calm",5],["compose",3],["comfort",2],["active",1],["little",6],["silence",0],["lull",3],["order",2],["usual",6],["smooth",0]],"en":"After the storm the sea went quiet, and a smooth calm spread over the water. My father, who is not usually a still man, sat on the wall and said nothing. It is a lull, he told me, not a silence. The little harbour was in good order again, and the boats lay at rest in it. He is active all day and does not know how to compose himself, but on that evening he found comfort in just sitting. I did not disturb him; I only watched the light move.","zh":"暴风雨过后，海静了下来，一片平顺的安宁铺在水面上。我爸平时不是个能静住的人，那天却坐在墙上什么也不说。他告诉我：这只是暂时的平息，不是真正的寂静。小港湾又整整齐齐了，船都安安静静停在里头。他一天到晚闲不住，不知道该怎么让自己沉下来，可那天晚上，光是坐着就让他觉得宽慰。我没去打扰他，只是看着光线一点点移动。"},"raise":{"tw":[["climb",0],["carry",3],["bet",2],["lower",1],["pay",6],["farm",0],["draw",3],["better",2],["benefit",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The men on the farm had to raise the new barn before the winter. They would climb the frame with a rope, carry each beam up by hand, and draw it into place. One of them made a bet that he could lift the heaviest piece alone, and lost. The owner agreed to pay them better for the extra days, because the benefit to the whole village was clear. In the evening they lit a fire by the road and talked about the year to come. Nobody mentioned the lower price of grain.","zh":"农场上的那些人得赶在入冬前把新谷仓立起来。他们拿绳子爬上架子，把每根梁用手抬上去，再拉到位。有一个人打赌说他一个人能抬起最重的那根，结果输了。东家答应对多加的这几天给更好的工钱，因为这对整个村子都有好处，谁都看得见。傍晚他们在路边生了一堆火，聊起明年。没人提粮价走低的事。"},"record":{"tw":[["book",3],["card",3],["list",2],["erase",1],["consecutive",6],["enter",0],["cut",3],["save",2],["straight",6],["read",0]],"en":"The clerk kept a record of every visitor in a thick book by the door. She would enter the name, read the card, and then write a straight list of the hours each one stayed. No two entries were consecutive; the numbers jumped about all day. If she made a mistake she would erase it with a small knife and cut the page away. I save these, she said, because one day someone will want to know who came and went. She has kept the same record for thirty years.","zh":"门房在门边一本厚本子里记下每个来访的人。她会写下名字，看一眼证件，然后把每人待了几个钟头一行行直着列出来。没有两条是挨着的，一整天数字都在乱跳。要是写错了，她就用小刀刮掉，把那一块裁下来。她说：这些我都留着，总有一天有人想知道谁来过、谁走了。同一本记录她记了三十年。"},"remember":{"tw":[["think",0],["mind",3],["mention",2],["forget",1],["maybe",6],["recall",0],["qualify",3],["associate",2],["imagine",6],["retrieve",0]],"en":"I cannot always remember names, but I can recall a face for years. My mother would mention someone at dinner and I would think, without being able to qualify it, that I had met them before. Maybe that is why I associate certain rooms with certain people. I try to imagine what my grandfather looked like, and I can still retrieve the sound of his voice. What I forget is small: the day, the street, the colour of the door. He said once that the mind keeps what matters and lets the rest go.","zh":"我不总能记住名字，但一张脸我能记好些年。饭桌上我妈提到某人，我心里就会觉得以前见过，可说不清是怎么个见过法。也许正因如此，我总把某些屋子和某些人连在一块儿。我试着去想我爷爷长什么样，还能把他说话的声调捞回来。我忘掉的都是些小事：哪一天、哪条街、门是什么颜色。他生前说过，脑子留下来的都是要紧的，其余的全放走了。"},"ride":{"tw":[["drive",0],["boat",3],["climb",2],["walk",1],["bike",6],["sit",0],["bus",3],["continue",2],["track",6],["mount",0]],"en":"We used to ride the old bus up the valley every summer. My father would drive to the station, leave the car, and climb aboard with two bags. On the boat we would sit at the back and watch the track of white water behind us. Sometimes he would let me mount his bike and walk it along the road beside him. When the light began to go he would say we should continue a little further, and we always did. I have never found a journey I liked better.","zh":"每年夏天我们都坐那趟老旧的公共汽车上山谷去。我爸先开车到车站，把汽车留下，再拎着两个包爬上车。在船上我们就坐在船尾，看身后那道白色的水痕。有时候他让我骑上他的自行车，他在旁边推着走。天光开始暗下来时，他总说再往前一点吧，而我们每回都真的往前了。我后来再没遇到过比那更让我喜欢的旅程。"},"right":{"tw":[["good",0],["floor",3],["change",2],["left",1],["without",6],["proper",5],["access",3],["hand",2],["back",6],["correct",0]],"en":"The right to walk on that ground belonged to the village, but nobody had the proper papers. A man came from the city and put a fence across the path, so we had to go round by the left side of the hill. My grandfather said it was not good, and that without access to the water the farms would change hands within a year. He wrote to the council and got the correct answer at last: the fence came down. He kept the letter in his hand all the way home, and on the back he wrote the date. Then he laid it on the floor of the hall and read it to us twice.","zh":"在那片地上行走的权利本来是村里的，可谁手里都没有正式的文件。城里来了个人，在路当中拉起一道栅栏，我们只好绕到山左边走。我爷爷说这样不行，要是取不到水，这些农地一年之内就得易主。他给镇公所写了信，最后得了个正确的答复：栅栏拆了。他一路把那封信捏在手里回家，还在背面写下了日期。"},"rise":{"tw":[["climb",3],["head",3],["change",2],["fall",1],["decline",6],["grow",2],["wave",3],["look",2],["surge",6],["jump",3]],"en":"We climbed to the head of the valley to watch the sun rise. The price of grain had begun to decline that spring, and the farmers said the change would not last. They would look at the sky and guess, and when the wind came the wheat would wave like water. In a dry year the crop can grow quickly and then fall in a single night. My uncle said the worst thing was the surge of hope in June. Then he jumped the wall and went in for breakfast.","zh":"我们爬到山谷顶上去看日出。那年春天粮价开始往下走，种地的人说这变化长不了。他们会抬头看天、凭经验猜，风一来，麦子就像水一样起伏。碰上旱年，庄稼能长得飞快，然后一夜之间全倒。我叔说最难受的是六月里那阵子希望往上涌的时候。说完他跳过墙，进屋吃早饭去了。"},"round":{"tw":[["around",0],["bottom",3],["call",2],["square",1],["final",6],["beat",0],["rubbish",3],["change",2],["match",6],["attack",0]],"en":"The final round of the match was played in front of a small crowd. There is a square of grass at the bottom of our street, and the players had to walk around a rubbish bin to reach it. The drummer would beat his drum and call out the score after every point. Our side came under attack early, and the coach had to change the plan twice. It was a hard game, and by the end the whole team was too tired to speak. They lost, but the crowd stood up for them all the same.","zh":"比赛的最后一轮是在一小群观众面前踢的。我们这条街尽头有块方方的草地，球员得绕过一只垃圾桶才能走到场上。鼓手每得一分就敲鼓、报比分。我们这边一开场就被压着打，教练不得不两次改打法。那是场硬仗，到终场时整队人都累得说不出话。他们输了，可观众还是都站起来为他们鼓掌。"},"run":{"tw":[["carry",0],["cut",3],["break",2],["idle",1],["start",6],["course",0],["double",3],["change",2],["home",6],["draw",3]],"en":"My brother used to run the two miles home from school every day. He would cut across the field, break through the hedge, and arrive at the door with his shirt out. He never sat idle; if the weather was bad he would run the course indoors, up and down the stairs. He would draw a mark on the door frame after every run, and twice he ran a double distance on purpose, just to see what his body would do. Our mother would carry a glass of water out to him, and he would drink it standing up. That was the start of a habit that has never changed.","zh":"我哥哥从前每天从学校跑两英里回家。他抄过那片田，钻过树篱，到门口时衬衫都跑出来了。他从不闲坐着；天气不好就在屋里跑那条路线，楼上楼下地跑。每跑完一趟他就在门框上画一道记，还有两回他故意跑双倍的路，就想看看自己身体能扛成什么样。我妈会端杯水出去给他，他就站着喝。这个习惯从那时候起就没变过。"},"second":{"tw":[["back",0],["climax",3],["position",2],["first",1],["final",6],["bit",0],["pinpoint",3],["support",2],["straight",6],["minute",0]],"en":"She finished a very close second in the final race of the season. For a bit she stood at the back of the field and could not look at anyone. The climax had come in the first hundred metres, when she was still in a good position; after that the winner moved away and she could not pinpoint where she had lost the time. One minute, her coach said, and you would have had it. He asked her to hold her back straight and to support her weight on the other foot. She simply nodded.","zh":"赛季最后一场比赛，她以极小的差距拿了第二。有一小会儿，她站在场地最后头，谁也不敢看。最要紧的那一刻出现在头一百米，那时候她的位置还很好；之后领先的人跑远了，而她说不出自己是在哪儿丢掉了时间。她教练说：就差一分钟，你就拿下了。他让她把背挺直，把重心换到另一只脚上撑住。她只是点了点头。"},"sell":{"tw":[["deal",3],["clear",3],["exchange",2],["buy",1],["purchase",6],["trade",0],["market",3],["sale",2],["cash",6],["betray",0]],"en":"My father used to sell vegetables at the market on Saturday mornings. He would make one deal with the man on his left and a better one with the woman on his right, and by nine the best of the boxes were gone. He took cash and would not exchange a purchase without a receipt. Once you sell, he said, you must not betray the buyer by sending him a poor crate. He was in the trade for thirty years and never made a sale he could not stand behind. I remember him clearing the stall in the rain.","zh":"我爸从前星期六早上在集市上卖菜。他会跟左边那人讲一笔，再跟右边的女人讲一笔更好的，到九点最好的几箱就都出手了。他只收现钱，没有收据就不肯换货。他说：东西一旦卖出去，你就不能给买家发一箱烂的，那叫背叛人。他在这行做了三十年，没有一笔买卖是他不肯担的。我记得他在雨里收摊的样子。"},"set":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["bed",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["next",6],["dress",0],["charge",3],["choose",2],["break",6],["fit",0]],"en":"Every evening my grandmother would set the table before the sun began to rise. She would arrange the plates in a row, choose the bread, and then dress the salad with oil. When the heat came on she had to charge the old cooker and wait for it to fit the temperature she wanted. The next thing was the bed, which she made with a stiff cover. Nothing would make her change the order: set the table first, break the bread last. It was the same in every house she ever lived in.","zh":"每天傍晚，太阳还没下去，我奶奶就把桌子摆好了。她把盘子排成一行，挑好面包，再给沙拉浇上油。暖气一上来，她就得给那台老灶添料，等着它到她要的温度。接下来是床，她用的是硬挺的床罩。什么也改不了她那套顺序：先摆桌，最后才掰面包。她住过的每一间屋子都是这样。"},"show":{"tw":[["express",0],["finger",3],["appear",2],["hide",1],["watch",6],["picture",0],["fly",3],["inform",2],["film",6],["present",0]],"en":"The teacher wanted to show us how a moth hides from a bird. She would hold up a picture, then point one finger at the shape on the wall. Watch closely, she said, and you will see it appear and then vanish. She had a short film on an old machine, and she used it to express the same idea in another way. Her aim was to inform, not to amuse us. At the end she asked each of us to present one thing we had learned, and then let a moth fly out of the window.","zh":"老师想让我们看看飞蛾是怎么躲开鸟的。她会举起一张图，再用一根手指点着墙上那个形状。她说：看仔细了，你会看见它先出现，然后又不见。她还有一部旧机器放的短片，就用它把同一个意思换个法子讲了一遍。她的目的是让我们知道些什么，不是逗我们乐。最后她让我们每人讲一件学到的事，然后把一只蛾子从窗口放了出去。"},"side":{"tw":[["face",0],["edge",3],["cut",2],["bottom",3],["rest",6],["position",0],["front",3],["line",2],["back",6],["slope",0]],"en":"Our house stands on the side of a hill, with a steep slope at the front. If you look at its face from the road, you see a line of small windows and a door at the bottom of three steps. On the back side there is a bench where my father likes to rest. He will cut the grass along the edge of the path and then sit down with his back to the wall. From that position he can watch everyone who comes up the road. It is the best seat in the village, he says.","zh":"我们家在山坡上，前面是一道陡坡。你要是从路上看它的门脸，会看到一排小窗，还有三级台阶底下的一扇门。背面有条长凳，我爸喜欢在那儿歇着。他会沿着路边把草剪齐，然后背靠着墙坐下。从那个位置，他看得见每个上坡来的人。他说，这是全村最好的位子。"},"sit":{"tw":[["ride",0],["lounge",3],["serve",2],["lie",1],["wait",6],["seat",0],["perch",3],["travel",2],["stay",6],["model",0]],"en":"On long journeys my aunt would rather sit than lie down. She says that in a lounge car you can watch the country travel past, and that a comfortable seat is worth any amount of money. She used to ride the night train to the coast and perch on a small stool by the window for hours. A waiter would come to serve coffee, and she would stay there until dawn. She has never learned to rest in a bed on a train. I am not a model of good sense, she says, but I do not miss much.","zh":"长途旅行的时候，我姑姑宁可坐着也不肯躺下。她说在休息车厢里能看着乡野往后走，一个舒服的座位值多少钱都行。她从前常坐夜车去海边，一连几个钟头就栖在窗边一张小凳上。服务员会过来送咖啡，她就在那儿一直待到天亮。她始终学不会在火车卧铺上歇着。她说：我不是什么明白人的榜样，但我没漏掉多少东西。"},"slow":{"tw":[["behind",0],["delay",3],["decrease",2],["fast",1],["pace",6],["easy",0],["clog",3],["decelerate",2],["steady",6],["dim",0]],"en":"The traffic was slow all the way out of the city. A single broken lorry had begun to clog the road, and the pace of every car behind it fell to a walk. My father kept a steady voice, but he would not drive fast in the dim light. There is no need to delay anyone, he said, and no harm in being a little behind. When the road opened his worry decreased slowly, and then the speed picked up again. He told me that an easy journey is one where you never have to decelerate suddenly.","zh":"出城的路上一直堵得很慢。一辆坏了的货车把路堵住了，跟在它后面每辆车的速度都降到步行的样子。我爸声音很稳，但天色昏暗他不肯开快。他说：没必要耽误别人，落在后面一点也没什么坏处。路一通，他的担心慢慢消下来，车速也就重新提起来了。他还告诉我，一趟舒服的行程，就是你从来不用猛地减速。"},"start":{"tw":[["begin",2],["birth",3],["act",2],["finish",1],["next",6],["first",0],["fall",3],["leave",2],["break",6],["jump",0]],"en":"The race would start at the first light, and by then the whole village was awake. My cousin had trained all year for it, and he meant to finish in the top ten. At the next bend the road begins to fall away, so the runners have to take it easy or they break their step. I watched him leave the gate and jump the low wall at the corner. It was the birth of something new in him, I think. He said afterwards that the act of starting is the only part that ever frightened him.","zh":"比赛天一亮就开始，到那时候全村人都醒了。我表哥为这场赛跑练了一整年，一心想跑进前十。下一个转弯处路面开始往下斜，所以跑的人得悠着点，不然步子就乱了。我看着他从大门出去，跳过拐角那道矮墙。我觉得，那是他心里有什么新东西生出来了。后来他说，真正让他害怕的只有起跑那一下。"},"stop":{"tw":[["bar",0],["call",3],["act",2],["start",1],["move",6],["break",3],["close",3],["stay",2],["prevent",6],["catch",2]],"en":"The bus makes one stop at the end of our road, and if you do not catch it there you must walk. The driver will call out the name of the place and then close the doors. There is a metal bar across the front window, and a small sign that says you must not stay on after the last stop of the day. In winter the ice can prevent the bus from moving at all, and then my mother has to act quickly and find another way to get to work. The rain began to break just as we started out.","zh":"公共汽车在我们这条路尽头有一站，要是在那儿没赶上，就只能走路了。司机报出地名，然后关门。前窗上横着一根金属杆，还有块小牌子写着：到当天最后一站后不得继续留在车上。冬天结冰能让车根本动不了，那时候我妈就得赶紧想办法，另外找路去上班。我们刚出发，雨就开始小下来了。"},"tail":{"tw":[["behind",0],["tree",3],["cut",2],["head",1],["nose",6],["bottom",0],["brush",3],["end",2],["snout",6],["dog",0]],"en":"My dog will run in circles and chase his own tail until he falls over. He is a small thing with a black nose and a wet snout, and he keeps his head down when he is working. At the bottom of the garden there is an old tree, and he likes to sit behind it. I have to brush him every week and cut the hair that grows long at the end of his back. He watches me with his tail still, waiting for the brush to come near him again.","zh":"我的狗会绕着圈跑，追自己的尾巴，一直追到摔倒。它个头小，黑鼻子，鼻头总是湿的，干活的时候脑袋低着。园子尽头有一棵老树，它喜欢坐在树后面。我每个星期都得给它刷毛，把脊背末端长出来的毛剪掉。它尾巴一动不动地盯着我，等刷子再靠近它。"},"top":{"tw":[["clear",0],["head",3],["complete",2],["bottom",1],["key",6],["cover",0],["tail",3],["degree",2],["hold",6],["lead",0]],"en":"We climbed to the top of the hill on a clear morning. My brother held the key to the gate in his hand and would not let go of it. At the bottom of the slope a road led away to the next town, and above our heads the cover of cloud began to lift. A dog ran past us with its tail up, and we watched it go. He wanted to complete the walk before noon, so we had to hold a good speed. It was, to a high degree, the best morning of that whole year.","zh":"一个晴朗的早晨，我们爬到了山顶。我弟弟手里攥着大门的钥匙，怎么都不肯放。坡底下有条路通向邻镇，我们头顶上的云层开始散开。一条狗翘着尾巴从我们身边跑过，我们看着它跑远。他想在中午前走完这趟，所以我们得保持一个不错的速度。那真是那一年里最好的一个早晨，好得没法说。"},"wake":{"tw":[["heat",0],["call",3],["change",2],["sleep",1],["fall",6],["awake",0],["ferment",3],["island",2],["fear",6],["arouse",0]],"en":"The heat would wake me before six every morning that summer, and I would lie still and try to sleep again. My father would call from the yard, then fall quiet, waiting for me to come down. On the island there was nothing to fear and nothing to hurry for. The change came slowly: by August I was awake at five without any noise at all, and I began to ferment ideas about what I would do when we went home. He could arouse me with a single word. Years later I still wake at that hour, and the old house comes back to me in the dark.","zh":"那年夏天，每天早上六点不到，热气就把我叫醒了，我就躺着不动，想再睡一会儿。我爸会在院子里喊我，然后安静下来，等我下楼。在岛上没什么可怕的，也没什么要赶的。变化是慢慢来的：到了八月，我五点就醒，一点动静都不用，脑子里开始发酵起回家以后要干什么的念头。他一个字就能把我叫起来。很多年以后我还是那个点醒，那栋老房子就在黑里回到我眼前。"},"waste":{"tw":[["blow",0],["burn",3],["act",2],["conserve",1],["water",6],["wild",0],["rubbish",3],["kill",2],["garbage",6],["rot",0]],"en":"It is a waste to burn good wood in an open fire, and my father would not act so foolishly. He told us to conserve what we had and never to let food rot in the box. The wild part of the garden was full of rubbish and old garbage, and he made us clear it every spring. If a storm should blow down a tree, we had to cut it up that week or the water would get in and kill the wood. He said a house that lets things go is a house that is already lost.","zh":"在明火上烧好木头是浪费，我爸不会干这种蠢事。他叫我们省着用手里有的，别让吃食在箱子里烂掉。园子荒着的那半边净是垃圾和烂七八糟的旧东西，他每年春天都逼我们去清一遍。要是风把树刮倒了，我们得在那个星期里把它锯开，不然水汽钻进去，木头就废了。他说，一栋什么都撒手不管的房子，其实早就没了。"},"wind":{"tw":[["lead",0],["ball",3],["move",2],["unwind",1],["rain",6],["lift",0],["clue",3],["raise",2],["water",6],["nose",0]],"en":"The wind came up the valley just before the rain started. My uncle had to lead the boat round, and my job was to raise the sail and keep the nose of it into the weather. There was no clue where the storm would move next. A ball of grey cloud sat on the hills and would not lift. When it was over I would unwind the wet rope and hang it on the fence. Over the water afterwards there was a fine line of foam as far as I could see.","zh":"雨还没下，风就先顺着山谷上来了。我叔得把船领回去，我的活儿是把帆升起来，让船头迎着风。谁也说不准风暴接下来往哪儿挪。山上蹲着一团灰云，怎么也不肯散。事后我把湿绳子解开绕松，挂在栅栏上。那之后水面上拉着一条细白的泡沫，一眼望不到头。"},"cat":{"tw":[["feline",4],["guy",0],["man",2],["dog",6],["sick",0],["woman",2],["rabbit",6],["cast",0]],"en":"The woman next door keeps a cat that has never once been friendly to me. She says it is a feline thing, and that a dog would be easier, but she is fond of it. There is a man down the road who swears he saw it cast a shadow on the wall like a person. Once, when the animal was sick, she would not leave the house for a week. My brother, who is a quiet guy, says the rabbit in our garden is the reason it comes over our fence so often.","zh":"隔壁那位女士养了一只猫，那猫从来没对我友好过。她说这是猫的天性，还说养条狗会省事些，可她就是喜欢它。路那头有个男人一口咬定，说他见过这猫在墙上投下一个像人一样的影子。有一回这猫病了，她整整一个星期没出门。我弟弟是个安静的人，他说我们园子里那只兔子，就是它总翻过篱笆过来的原因。"},"cause":{"tw":[["causal",4],["drive",0],["bring",3],["origin",2],["risk",6],["engine",3],["venture",2],["result",6]],"en":"Nobody could say what the cause of the fire had been. The engine of the old car was cold, and there was no sign of anyone in the yard. My father said the most likely origin was a wire under the floor, though he admitted that was only a guess. He would not risk another night in the house, so he asked me to drive to my aunt's. She asked him to bring the papers with him, and he did not venture an opinion again until the morning. The result of the inquiry was the same: no clear reason. He said a causal chain like that is easy to see afterwards and impossible to see at the time.","zh":"没人说得清那场火是因何而起的。旧车的发动机是凉的，院子里也没有人来过的痕迹。我爸说最可能起头的地方是地板下的一根电线，不过他也承认这只是猜的。他不肯再在这屋里冒险住一晚，于是我们开车去了姑姑家。她叫他把文件带上，他一晚上没再开口说什么，直到第二天早上。查问的结果还是一样：没有明确的原因。他说，这样的因果链，事后看得清，当时看不见。"},"dress":{"tw":[["dresser",4],["clip",0],["change",3],["cook",2],["wear",6],["coat",3],["finish",2],["attire",6]],"en":"My mother would dress for dinner even when there was nobody to see her. She would change out of her working clothes, clip her hair back, and put on a dark coat. She would wear the same one for twenty years. Her attire never changed with fashion. Then she would cook, and the finish of the meal always mattered more to her than the dress itself. The dresser in her room still holds the same things: a comb, a pin, and a photograph of her mother in a dress of pale blue.","zh":"哪怕没人看，我妈吃晚饭也要换身体面的衣服。她脱下干活的衣裳，把头发别上去，再穿上一件深色外套。同一件她一穿就是二十年。她的穿戴从不跟着时兴走。然后她去做饭，而对她来说，一顿饭最后收得好不好，比身上这条裙子要紧得多。她房里的梳妆台里还是那几样东西：一把梳子、一根别针，还有一张她母亲穿浅蓝裙子的照片。"},"mother":{"tw":[["maternal",4],["father",1],["care",2],["daughter",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["husband",6],["fuss",0]],"en":"My mother was the quiet one in our house; my father made all the noise. She had a maternal way with every child on the street, and she would care for them as if they were her own. When my sister had a daughter of her own, my mother went to stay for a month and would not let anyone else take over. She and my father had been husband and wife for forty years, and she still made a fuss over his birthday. She used to say that a parent is not a person who generates rules but one who keeps them company.","zh":"在我们家，我妈是安静的那个，闹出动静的全是我爸。她对街上每个孩子都有股母性，会像对自己孩子一样照顾他们。我姐姐生下自己的女儿以后，我妈过去住了一个月，不让别人插手。她和我爸做了四十年夫妻，她还照样为他的生日忙前忙后。她生前常说，当父母不是定规矩的人，而是陪着他们的人。"},"person":{"tw":[["personify",4],["individual",0],["creature",3],["man",6],["soul",0],["tyrant",3],["woman",6],["mortal",0]],"en":"He was the kind of person who remembers your name after one meeting. My grandfather used to personify patience for me: he would let a man talk for an hour and never once look at the clock. He said that no individual is only one thing, and that the worst creature in the village had a soul as well. He had lived under a tyrant in his youth, and it had taught him to be gentle with every woman and man he met. He was, for all his faults, the most mortal and the most decent of us.","zh":"他见过一面就能记住你的名字，就是这种人。在我眼里，我爷爷简直就是耐心的化身：他能让人讲上一个钟头，一眼都不看钟。他说，没有哪一个人只是一样东西，村里最坏的家伙也有一颗心。他年轻时在暴君底下活过，这让他对遇见的每个女人男人都和和气气。他毛病不少，可他是我们当中最像个凡人、也最厚道的一个。"},"song":{"tw":[["sing",4],["strain",0],["carol",3],["sound",2],["pop",6],["vocal",0],["anthem",3],["tune",6]],"en":"My aunt could sing anything, from a carol at Christmas to a pop song on the radio. She had a strong vocal line and could hold a tune for a whole verse without effort. When the old anthem was played at the village meeting, she stood up and the sound of her voice filled the hall. She said she had learned it all by ear, and that a strain of music heard once was enough for her. She never sang for money. At the end of the evening the whole room would ask her for one more, and she always gave it.","zh":"我姑姑什么都能唱，从圣诞的颂歌到收音机里流行的曲子。她嗓子很稳，一整段调子不用费劲就能托住。村里聚会上放那首老颂歌的时候，她站起来，她的声音把整个礼堂都填满了。她说她全是听会的，一段曲子只要听过一遍就够她用了。她从不为钱唱。晚上快结束时，满屋的人都会再要一首，她从来没推过。"},"tend":{"tw":[["tender",4],["run",0],["garden",3],["attend",2],["alike",6],["lean",0],["suffer",3],["incline",0]],"en":"My grandmother used to tend the garden in the mornings, before anyone else was up. She would lean on her stick to reach the far bed, and she had a tender way with young plants that I have never been able to copy. She had to attend to the roses first, then run a hose along the wall. She said that all living things are alike in this: they suffer when they are forgotten. I incline to think she was right. In July the garden gave back more than she could eat, and she would leave boxes of it at the gate.","zh":"我奶奶从前每天早上都照料园子，比别人起得都早。她会撑着棍子去够最远那畦，对嫩苗那份轻柔劲儿，我怎么学也学不来。她得先照看玫瑰，再顺墙拉一条水管浇水。她说所有活物在这一点上都一样：没人管，就受苦。我也倾向认为她是对的。到了七月，园子里长出来的东西她根本吃不完，就把一箱箱菜放在大门口。"},"will":{"tw":[["willing",4],["leave",0],["remember",3],["decide",2],["testament",0],["devise",3],["purpose",2],["bequeath",0]],"en":"My great-uncle was a man of strong will and few words. He was willing to help anyone, but he would not be told what to do. When he could no longer leave the house, he decided to write his testament himself, and he would remember every cousin by name. He devised a simple plan: the land to his son, the tools to the man who had worked for him longest. He said his purpose was only to avoid a quarrel after he was gone. He would bequeath nothing that could be argued over.","zh":"我叔公是个意志很硬、话很少的人。他愿意帮任何人的忙，但谁也别想指挥他。到出不了门的时候，他决定自己写遗嘱，还把每个表亲的名字都记得清清楚楚。他定了个简单的方案：地给儿子，工具给跟他干得最久的那个伙计。他说他的用意只是免得自己走以后有人吵架。凡是可能被人争的东西，他一件都不留。"},"address":{"tw":[["call",0],["ask",3],["use",2],["message",6],["cover",0],["approach",3],["access",2],["public",6],["deal",0]],"en":"The chairman had to address a room of two hundred people, and he was not used to it. He would call a name, ask a question, and then wait too long for an answer. His message was simple, but he had to cover a great deal of ground before he came to it. He had no access to the figures, so he had to approach the problem from the side. It was a public meeting, and by the end even the people at the back had understood what he wanted.","zh":"主席得对着一屋子两百号人讲话，他不习惯这个。他会点一个名字，问一个问题，然后等答案等得太久。他要说的其实很简单，可走到正题之前得铺陈好大一片。他手头没有数据，只好从侧面去谈这个问题。那是一场公开的会，到散场时，连最后一排的人也知道他要的是什么了。"},"ask":{"tw":[["need",0],["call",3],["address",2],["tell",6],["demand",2],["cost",3],["communicate",2],["want",6],["require",0]],"en":"If you need to ask a favour of my father, you should call him in the evening and tell him plainly what you want. He does not like a long speech. He will demand to know the cost before he agrees to anything, and he will require you to say when you need it. He is not easy to address on the phone, because he does not like to communicate in that way. But once he has said yes, he will not go back on it. That, to him, is what an honest answer means.","zh":"你要是有事求我爸，就在晚上给他打电话，直截了当跟他说你要什么。他不爱听长篇大论。答应任何事之前，他都要先问清代价，还得让你说准什么时候要。在电话里跟他说话不容易，因为他不喜欢用这种方式交流。可一旦他点头，就不会反悔。在他看来，说一句实在话就是这个意思。"},"ball":{"tw":[["egg",0],["football",3],["dance",2],["kick",6],["lump",0],["bowl",3],["wind",2],["catch",6],["formal",0]],"en":"My cousin played football every Saturday and could catch almost anything with one hand. Before a game he would eat two eggs and a bowl of rice, and then kick a ball against the wall for an hour. After the game there was a dance at the club, and he had to wear something formal for it, which he hated. He was never good at that side of things. In a hard wind he would stand with his hands in his pockets and roll a small lump of bread between his fingers.","zh":"我表哥每个星期六都踢球，几乎什么东西单手都能接住。比赛前他会吃两个鸡蛋、一碗米饭，然后对着墙踢一个小时球。比赛结束后俱乐部有舞会，他得穿点正式的衣裳，他讨厌这个。这方面他从来不行。刮大风的时候，他就把手插在兜里站着，指头间搓着一小块面包。"},"bar":{"tw":[["cake",0],["close",3],["room",2],["shop",6],["stop",0],["save",3],["support",2],["block",2]],"en":"There is a small bar at the corner of our street, and the man who keeps it knows everyone. He will close the shop at eleven, wipe the bar, and put a cake under a glass cover for the morning. People come in to stop for a while and talk about the weather in the back room. He has one rule: if you cannot support yourself on the stool, you have had enough. In winter the snow can block the door, and he will not let anyone save him the trouble of clearing it himself.","zh":"我们街角有个小酒吧，看店的那个人认识所有人。他十一点打烊，把吧台擦干净，再把一块蛋糕搁在玻璃罩下留着早上。人们进来歇一会儿，在里屋聊聊天气。他有一条规矩：你要是坐都坐不稳，那就是喝够了。冬天下雪能把门堵住，他不让别人替他省这份力气，自己扫。"},"bear":{"tw":[["accept",3],["deal",3],["act",2],["bull",1],["little",6],["birth",0],["drop",3],["big",6],["carry",3]],"en":"There was a bear in the woods above the village that summer, a big one with a little cub. The farmers would not accept it; they said it would deal with the sheep the way a bull deals with a fence. My father had to act fast, so he and two others went up with a lamp and a gun. They did not shoot. They watched the mother carry her cub across the stream and drop into the dark on the far side. He said afterwards that he had seen a birth and a death in the same minute, and that he would not go up there again.","zh":"那年夏天，村子上头的林子里来了一只熊，个头很大，带着一只小崽。种地的人不肯认这事，说它对付羊就像公牛对付栅栏一样。我爸得赶紧行动，于是他和另外两个人提着灯、带着枪上了山。他们没有开枪。他们看着母熊把小崽叼过溪水，落到对岸的黑地里去。事后他说，他在同一分钟里看见了生和死，以后再也不上去了。"},"beat":{"tw":[["dead",0],["full",3],["move",2],["upset",6],["pound",0],["kill",3],["play",2],["win",6],["round",0]],"en":"You could hear the beat of the drum from the far end of the field. It was a full band, and the players had to move with the music or lose the round. My brother was upset before the match; he said his legs felt dead and heavy. He began to pound the ball against the wall to warm up, and after ten minutes he could play again. In the last minute they managed to win, and the crowd made a noise like a heart beating. It was the sort of afternoon that could kill a man's nerve, and he came through it.","zh":"从场地那头就能听见鼓点。那是个满编的乐队，球员得跟着音乐动，不然这一轮就丢了。比赛前我弟弟心里发慌，他说两条腿又沉又死。他开始对着墙猛砸球热身，十分钟以后又能踢了。最后一分钟他们赢了，看台上的声浪像心跳一样。那种下午最能毁掉一个人的胆气，而他从里面走了出来。"},"bed":{"tw":[["bottom",0],["course",3],["plant",2],["room",6],["love",0],["lift",3],["supply",2],["bare",6],["bang",0]],"en":"The bed in my room stood under the window, and in summer I could see the bottom of the garden from it. Of course it was too small for me by the time I was fifteen, and my feet hung over the end. On the far side there was a bare wall where my mother had tried to plant a rose that never grew. She would lift the mattress every spring to air it, and she kept a small supply of clean sheets in a box underneath. In winter the wind would bang the shutter against the frame all night, and I would love it.","zh":"我屋里的床摆在窗下，夏天我能从床上看见园子的尽头。当然，到我十五岁它就太小了，脚都搭在床沿外。对面是一堵光墙，我妈曾在那儿试着种一棵玫瑰，没活。每年春天她都会把床垫抬起来晾一晾，床底下的箱子里存着一小摞干净床单。冬天风整夜把窗板拍在框上，我倒很喜欢。"},"bill":{"tw":[["card",0],["check",3],["advertise",2],["repeal",6],["charge",0],["menu",3],["list",2],["tax",6],["note",0]],"en":"The bill came to more than we had expected, and my father asked to see the menu again. He would check every item on the list, note the charge for the bread, and then take out his card. The owner had begun to advertise a new tax on the board outside, and my father said a good council would repeal it within the year. He paid without another word and left the note on the table. On the way home he told me that a bill is a promise written down, and that it should be read twice.","zh":"账单比我们预想的高，我爸要求再看一遍菜单。他把单子上的每一顶都核了一遍，记下面包收的那笔钱，然后掏出卡。店主已经在外面板子上开始宣传一项新税，我爸说，一个像样的议会一年之内就会把它废掉。他一句话没说就付了钱，纸条留在桌上。回家路上他跟我说，账单就是写下来的承诺，得读两遍。"},"blow":{"tw":[["snow",0],["box",3],["lay",2],["attempt",6],["waste",0],["burn",3],["move",2],["pull",6],["bump",0]],"en":"The wind began to blow hard in the night and the snow came with it. In the morning the whole lane was under a white cover, and my father had to pull on his boots and move the car out of the way. There was a bump in the road that nobody could see, and it took him three attempts to get past it. He would burn the old boxes in the yard rather than waste them, and then lay a plank over the gap so the milkman could get through.","zh":"夜里起大风，雪跟着来了。早上整条小路都盖在白色底下一层，我爸只好蹬上靴子把车挪开。路上有个谁都看不见的坎，他试了三回才过去。他宁可把旧木箱在院子里烧掉，也不肯白白扔了，然后铺一块板子盖住坑，好让送牛奶的能过。"},"bother":{"tw":[["pain",0],["harass",3],["affect",2],["guess",6],["trouble",0],["plague",3],["confuse",2],["hurry",6],["devil",0]],"en":"It did not bother my grandmother that the tap dripped all night; she said a small trouble was better than a silent house. The pain in her knee would affect her in the mornings, and she would have to hurry less than she wanted to. I guess she was lonely, though she would never say so. The neighbours began to harass her about the garden, and one of them, a real devil of a man, would plague her every week. It only seemed to confuse her that anyone should mind so much.","zh":"水龙头整夜滴水，我奶奶一点不烦；她说有点小麻烦总比静得没声的屋子好。早上膝盖的疼会影响她，她想赶也赶不起来。我猜她是孤单的，虽然她从不这么说。邻居开始为园子的事来烦她，其中有个真像恶鬼一样的男人，每个星期都来缠她。别人这么在意，反倒让她摸不着头脑。"},"bring":{"tw":[["add",0],["return",3],["change",2],["help",6],["land",3],["fetch",3],["attract",2],["need",6],["play",0]],"en":"Every Sunday my uncle would bring the boat back to the harbour and bring the nets with him. He would return the key to the office, add a line to the list on the wall, and then fetch his bicycle. The land around the harbour had begun to change, and the new houses would attract people who had no need of a boat at all. He said he would help anyone who asked, but he would not play along with the council. In the end he sold up and moved inland.","zh":"每个星期天，我叔都把船带回港里，顺便把网也带回来。他把钥匙还给办公室，在墙上那张单子上添一行，然后去取自行车。港口周围的地开始变了，新盖的房子会招来那些根本用不着船的人。他说谁开口求他他都帮，但他不陪着镇公所作戏。最后他把东西都卖了，搬到了内地。"},"build":{"tw":[["figure",0],["lock",3],["better",2],["construct",6],["form",0],["raise",3],["body",2],["develop",6],["shape",0]],"en":"They had to build the new shed before the winter, and there was little time. The figure on the plan was simple, but nobody could agree on the form it should take. They would raise the walls first, then lock the two halves together with a long bar. My father said they would have to develop the design as they went, and change its shape twice before it was right. In the end the body of the shed was stronger than the old house, and better built, too. He had watched men construct barns all his life, and he knew that a good frame is never hurried.","zh":"他们得在入冬前把新棚子盖起来，时间不多。图上的尺寸很简单，可谁也说不准该做成什么形状。他们先把墙立起来，再用一根长杆把两半锁在一起。我爸说设计得边干边改，形状换了两回才对。最后棚子的主体比那栋老房子还结实，活儿也干得更好。他这辈子看着人盖谷仓，知道好架子从来不是赶出来的。"},"burn":{"tw":[["cut",0],["flame",3],["feel",2],["smoke",6],["fire",0],["blaze",3],["pain",2],["tear",6],["bite",0]],"en":"The fire in the field began to burn along the dry grass and the smoke could be seen from the road. My uncle had to cut a strip of ground to stop it, and by the time he had finished he could feel the heat through his boots. A single flame had started the whole blaze. He had a bad burn on one hand, and the pain kept him awake. It made his eyes tear. He said it was nothing, but he could not hold a cup without biting his lip.","zh":"地里的火顺着干草烧起来，从路上就能看见烟。我叔得先割出一条空地把它拦住，等他割完，隔着靴子都能感觉到烫。整场大火是从一簇火苗起的。他一只手烧伤了，疼得整夜睡不着，眼睛都给熏出泪来。他说没事，可是端起杯子就忍不住咬嘴唇。"},"call":{"tw":[["address",2],["bet",3],["ask",2],["answer",6],["cry",0],["double",3],["guess",2],["talk",6],["promise",0]],"en":"My father had to make one call and then he would leave the office. He asked for the number, gave his address, and waited for an answer. Then he had a long talk with a man he had worked with for years, and they made a bet about which of them would retire first. He could not guess his own luck well enough to double the stake. As he put the phone down he heard a cry from the street. He had promised to be home by six, and it was already past six.","zh":"我爸打完一个电话就要下班了。他问了号码，报了自己的地址，等着对方接。接着他跟一个共事多年的男人聊了很久，两人还打赌看谁先退休。他摸不准自己的运气，不敢把赌注翻倍。放下电话时，他听见街上一声喊叫。他早就答应六点前到家，可已经过六点了。"},"can":{"tw":[["behind",0],["head",3],["room",2],["able",6],["bottom",0],["retire",3],["remove",2],["need",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The can of paint stood at the bottom of the shelf behind the door, and nobody in the room seemed able to reach it. My grandfather would need a ladder, or he would have to remove the boxes in front. He would not retire until he had done the job himself, and he was not going to ask anyone. He put his head round the corner, took a long breath, and lifted the can down. There is no need for a fire, he said. It is only paint. Then he carried it out to the yard.","zh":"那罐油漆放在门后架子的最下层，屋里好像谁也没本事够到它。我爷爷要么得找把梯子，要么得把前面的箱子挪开。活儿没自己干完他是不肯收手的，也不打算开口求人。他把头探过拐角，长吸一口气，把那罐子端了下来。他说：用不着生火，就是油漆而已。然后他把它拎到院子里去了。"},"care":{"tw":[["charge",0],["mother",3],["control",2],["benefit",6],["concern",0],["nurse",3],["help",2],["medical",6],["deal",0]],"en":"My mother gave up her job to take care of my grandmother, and she did it for six years. She would deal with the nurse every morning, and she knew more about the medical side of it than any of the doctors. She had to control her own worry, because my grandmother could read a face at once. Her only concern was that the old woman should not feel a burden. She said there was no charge for what she did, and no benefit she wanted out of it. I never heard her ask anyone for help.","zh":"我妈辞了工作去照顾我奶奶，一照顾就是六年。每天早上她跟护士打交道，对这病医药方面的事，比哪个大夫都清楚。她还得管住自己的担心，因为我奶奶一眼就能看出人脸上的心思。她唯一在意的是别让老太太觉得自己是个累赘。她说她做的事不要钱，也不图什么好处。我从没听她开口求过谁帮忙。"},"chance":{"tw":[["find",0],["room",3],["try",2],["opportunity",6],["happen",0],["say",3],["measure",2],["hope",6],["luck",0]],"en":"There was a chance that the shop would close, and I wanted to find out before it happened. I went in and asked, and the woman said she would try to keep it open for another year. The room at the back was full of old stock, and the opportunity to sell it was small. You have to measure your hope, she said, and then take the luck that comes. I did not know what to say. I bought a book and left, and I still go back when I can.","zh":"这家店有可能要关，我想在它关掉之前弄清楚。我进去问了，那位女士说她会尽量再撑一年。里屋堆满了旧货，能卖出去的机会不大。她说：希望得掂量着来，然后来了运气就接住。我不知道该说什么。我买了一本书就走了，到现在有机会还回去看看。"},"charge":{"tw":[["bill",0],["bother",3],["change",2],["discharge",1],["criminal",6],["care",0],["check",3],["cost",2],["excite",0]],"en":"The charge against the man was serious, and nobody in the village wanted to talk about it. He was said to have set fire to a shop over a bill he could not pay, though the whole cost was small. The police had to discharge the case for lack of proof, and the criminal court never saw it. The change in the town afterwards was strange: people who had not bothered to speak to him before began to care what happened. I was excited and ashamed at the same time. My father told me to check my own books first.","zh":"对那个人的指控不轻，村里谁都不愿提这事。据说他为一笔付不起的账放火烧了一家店，其实总共也没多少钱。因为证据不足，警方只好撤了案，刑事法庭根本没审。之后镇上的变化很怪：先前连话都懒得跟他说的人，忽然开始关心起他的下场。我既兴奋又羞愧。我爸叫我先把自己那本账查清楚。"},"check":{"tw":[["agree",0],["card",3],["bill",2],["notice",6],["break",0],["catch",3],["change",2],["collect",6],["chip",0]],"en":"Before we paid, my mother would check the bill twice and then check it again. She would agree to nothing until she had seen the card in the window with the prices on it. There was a small notice by the door, and she read it while I waited. If the figures did not change, she would collect her bag and walk out without a word. My brother said she had a chip of ice where other people keep their patience. I took it as a break from the heat, and I did not catch her eye.","zh":"付钱之前，我妈要把账单核对两遍，然后再核一遍。没看见窗户上那张写着价钱的牌子，她什么都不会答应。门边有一张小告示，我等着的时候她把它读完了。数目要是不改，她就收拾起包，一声不响走出去。我弟说她身上那块地方别人都长着耐心，她长的是一块冰。我只当这是热天里歇口气，没敢跟她对上眼。"},"chip":{"tw":[["bit",0],["scale",3],["cut",2],["computer",6],["check",0],["splinter",3],["shape",2],["micro",6],["crisp",0]],"en":"There was a chip in the glass, a small bit of it missing at the edge, and it had a strange shape. I had to check it against the scale on the wall before I could say how deep the cut went. My father said the whole thing would break if we left it, so he took a splinter of wood and worked at it. He had a computer in the back room, and he used it to look up the price. A micro part of the surface was all that mattered. He said a crisp new one would cost too much.","zh":"玻璃上崩了一块，边上缺了小小一角，形状还挺怪。我得对着墙上的标尺量一下，才说得清那道口子有多深。我爸说这么放着整块都会裂，于是他拿了一根木片慢慢修。里屋有台电脑，他用它查了价钱。要紧的就是表面上极小的那一块。他说换一块又新又脆的要花太多钱。"},"clear":{"tw":[["clean",0],["approve",3],["change",2],["bounce",1],["without",6],["light",0],["commission",3],["empty",2],["open",0]],"en":"The water in the tank was clear again, and you could see the bottom of it in the light from the door. The man from the water commission came to approve the change we had made, and he said the whole job was clean work. He had to bounce a stone off the wall to test how hard it was. The room was empty except for a chair. We cannot go on without a proper cover, he said. Leave the lid open when you are finished. I wrote it down and he signed the paper.","zh":"水箱里的水又清了，顺着门口透进来的光能看见箱底。自来水委员会的那个人来查看我们做的改动，说这活儿干得干净。他用一块石头在墙上弹了一下，试试墙有多硬。屋里除了一把椅子什么都没有。他说：没有个像样的盖子，这么下去不行。收工的时候把盖子敞着。我记了下来，他在纸上签了字。"},"colour":{"tw":[["distort",0],["blue",3],["change",2],["palette",6],["gloss",0],["green",3],["interest",2],["bright",6],["tinge",0]],"en":"The colour of the sea changes ten times in a day, and no painter can hold it. My aunt would put a blue and a green on her palette and then add a tinge of grey, and by the afternoon the whole canvas had gone wrong. A photograph can distort what you saw, she said, and a gloss will hide the rest. Her real interest was in the light, not in the paint. The bright hours on the water were the ones she wanted. I watched her work for a whole summer and still cannot say how she did it.","zh":"海的颜色一天能变十回，哪个画画的都抓不住。我姑姑会在调色板上挤一坨蓝、一坨绿，再添一丝灰，到下午整幅画就全不对了。她说：照片会把你看见的东西扭歪，再上一层亮油就把剩下的都盖住了。她真正上心的是光，不是颜料。水面上那几段亮堂堂的时辰才是她想要的。我看她画了一整个夏天，到现在也说不出她是怎么画的。"},"company":{"tw":[["party",0],["chorus",3],["unit",2],["firm",6],["society",0],["cohort",3],["complement",2],["subsidiary",6],["accompany",0]],"en":"My father worked for a small firm for most of his life, and he was happy there. The company had one unit in the north and a subsidiary in another town, and he would have to accompany the manager on the long drive between them. At the office party each winter the whole cohort would stand up and sing in a chorus, badly. He said there was no better society than people who work well together. When a new man joined, my father told him he was a useful complement to the team, and meant it.","zh":"我爸大半辈子在一家小事务所做事，在那儿过得挺开心。这家公司北边有一个部门，另一个镇上还有家子公司，他得陪着经理在两头之间开长途。每年冬天公司聚会上，他们那一拨人都会站起来合唱，唱得很难听。他说再没有比一起把活干好的人更好的群体了。来了新人的时候，我爸会跟他说他是队里缺的那一块，而且是真心这么说的。"},"complete":{"tw":[["finish",0],["close",3],["end",2],["full",6],["over",0],["top",3],["fill",2],["entire",6],["perfect",0]],"en":"The work on the house was complete by the middle of June, and the whole family came to see it. We had to finish the top floor last, and it took a week to fill the gaps and close every door properly. The entire roof was new, and over the gate my father had put a small stone with the date on it. He said the house was not perfect, but it was full of light and it was ours. At the end of the day we sat in the yard and watched the sun go down.","zh":"房子到六月中就完工了，全家人都来看。顶楼是最后收的尾，光补缝、把每扇门关严实就用了一个星期。整个屋顶都是新的，大门上方我爸嵌了块小石头，上面刻着日期。他说这房子算不上十全十美，可是光线足，而且是咱们自己的。那天傍晚我们坐在院子里看太阳落下去。"},"concern":{"tw":[["care",0],["involve",3],["anxiety",2],["impact",6],["fear",0],["matter",3],["enterprise",2],["strong",6],["interest",2]],"en":"My uncle's only concern was that the enterprise should outlive him. He had built it from nothing, and he would involve himself in every small matter, from the price of wood to the colour of the sign. His anxiety before each winter was strong, and I came to share his fear of a bad season. He used to say that the impact of one bad year can undo ten good ones. He did not care much for money, but he cared a great deal about the interest of the people who worked for him.","zh":"我叔唯一放心不下的是这份事业得比他活得久。他是从一无所有把它做起来的，事无大小都要自己插手，从木料的价钱到招牌的颜色。每年入冬前他都格外焦虑，我也跟着他一起怕遇上坏年景。他生前常说，一个坏年头的折腾能把十个好年头搭进去。他对钱不怎么在意，可对跟着他干活那些人的利害，他上心得很。"},"control":{"tw":[["check",0],["card",3],["power",2],["system",6],["hold",0],["catch",3],["test",2],["force",6],["insure",0]],"en":"The control room was small and hot, and there was a card on the wall with the names of everyone who had ever worked there. You had to check the board every hour, and if a light went red you had to catch it at once. The whole system depended on one man keeping his hold on himself. The power came from two old wheels in the river below. A sudden force of water could test the best of them. They would insure the building against fire, but nothing could insure a man against his own temper. My father learned that in his first year and never forgot it.","zh":"控制室又小又热，墙上钉着一张卡片，写着所有在这儿干过活的人的名字。你得每小时查一次仪表盘，哪个灯变红了就得马上发现。整套系统全靠一个人把自己稳住。电从下面河里的两只旧水轮来。水势猛地一冲，最能干的人也经不住考。他们会给这楼保火险，可谁也没法给一个人的脾气保险。我爸头一年就懂了这一点，一辈子没忘。"},"cook":{"tw":[["fix",0],["brown",3],["change",2],["curry",6],["prepare",0],["dress",3],["cheat",2],["lamb",6],["ready",0]],"en":"My mother could cook anything, even a curry that my father said was the best he had ever eaten. She would prepare the lamb the night before, dress it with salt and herbs, and let it stand. In the morning she would brown it in a heavy pan and then change the heat. I used to fix the table while she worked, and I was never ready when she called. She said a cook who cheats with the timing will always be caught by the taste. Once a week she would let me stir the pot and tell me what to look for.","zh":"我妈什么都会做，有一道咖喱我爸说他一辈子没吃过更好的。她会头天晚上就把羊肉备好，撒上盐和香料，放着入味。第二天早上用厚锅把肉煎上色，再调火。她做饭的时候我就摆桌子，可每次她喊我，我都还没弄完。她说做菜的人在火候上偷懒，味道一定会把他揪出来。每个星期她会让我搅一次锅，告诉我该看什么。"},"course":{"tw":[["class",0],["round",3],["hunt",2],["long",6],["feed",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["beyond",6],["form",0]],"en":"I took a long course in woodwork one winter, and it was the best thing I ever did. There were twelve of us in the class, and the teacher would move from bench to bench and feed us advice in small amounts. In the first round he had us form a simple joint, and half of us made a waste of good timber. Beyond the window there was a field where he liked to hunt for old wood after a storm. It was the only course I ever finished. I still have the box I made in it, and the lid does not fit.","zh":"有一年冬天我上了一门很长的木工课，那是我做过最值的一件事。班上有十二个人，老师一个工作台一个工作台地走，一点一点给我们喂经验。头一轮他让我们做一个简单的榫接，我们一半人把好木料糟蹋了。窗外有块地，他一刮完风就爱去那儿捡旧木头。这是我唯一读完的一门课。我做的那只盒子还在，盖子合不上。"},"court":{"tw":[["romance",0],["chase",3],["act",2],["judge",6],["tribunal",0],["display",3],["room",2],["supreme",6],["courtyard",0]],"en":"The court sat in a small room at the back of the building, with a courtyard where the cars were parked. The judge came in, and everyone had to stand. It was not a supreme tribunal; it was a local matter about a fence. The two families had been in a long romance with the law, and each of them would display every paper they had ever signed. The younger son would chase the older one round the yard before the hearing began. It was hard to believe that any of it was meant to act as justice.","zh":"法庭设在楼后一间小屋里，外头是个停车的院子。法官进来，所有人都得站起来。这不是什么最高法院，只是为一堵篱笆闹的本地小事。这两家人跟法律纠缠了好些年，各自都愿意把签过的每一张纸摊出来。正式开庭前，小儿子还绕着院子追大儿子。很难相信这中间有哪一样是为了主持公道。"},"cover":{"tw":[["address",0],["coat",3],["dress",2],["short",6],["back",0],["course",3],["fire",2],["full",6],["continue",0]],"en":"The cover of the old book had come away at the back, and the address of a bookshop was written inside it in pencil. My mother would dress the torn corner with a piece of cloth, and then put a coat of thin glue along the spine. It took a short time to do, but it had to be done again every year. Of course she could not continue like that for ever. One winter evening, when the fire was full and the house was warm, she read the whole book aloud to me instead.","zh":"那本旧书的封面在书脊那边脱开了，里面用铅笔写着一家书店的地址。我妈会用一块布把撕破的角贴好，再沿着书脊抹一层薄胶。这花不了多少工夫，可每年都得再来一遍。她当然不能一直这样下去。有一个冬天的晚上，炉火正旺、屋里正暖，她索性把整本书念给我听了。"},"cross":{"tw":[["cover",2],["course",3],["meet",2],["along",6],["mark",0],["drive",3],["pass",2],["through",6],["track",0]],"en":"There is a stone cross at the place where two tracks meet, and you have to drive past it to reach the farm. We would walk along the field edge and then cross the stream at the old course. My father would mark the spot with a stick so we could find it again in the dark. As we came through the gate the rain began, and he put a cover over his head. It was a long pass of bad weather, and we were glad to see the light of the house.","zh":"两条小路交汇的地方立着一座石十字，开车去农场得从它旁边过。我们会沿着田边走过去，再从老河道那儿蹚过溪。我爸用一根树枝在那儿做个记号，好让我们黑天也能再找到。我们穿进大门的时候下起了雨，他把一块布顶在头上。这一阵坏天气拖得很久，远远看见屋里的灯，我们都松了口气。"},"cut":{"tw":[["burn",0],["check",3],["change",2],["drop",6],["issue",0],["kill",3],["free",2],["over",6],["track",0]],"en":"The cut on my hand was small but deep, and it would not stop bleeding. My mother had to check it twice, then change the cloth and hold it down hard. She said the cold could kill the feeling in my fingers, so she kept the fire going all night and would not let it burn out. In the morning the doctor had to cut the thread and set me free. No sport for a week, he said, and dropped the needle in the tray. I went back to the track the next day anyway, over the field behind the house. The issue never came up again.","zh":"我手上那道口子不大，可很深，血止不住。我妈核了两遍，换过布，又使劲按住。她说受凉会让手指头没了知觉，所以整夜守着炉子，不让火灭下去。早上去拆线，医生把线剪开，我就自由了。他说：一个星期不许运动，顺手把针丢进盘子里。第二天我照旧上了那条跑道，从屋后的田里绕过去。这事后来再没人提起。"},"deal":{"tw":[["address",0],["market",3],["act",2],["bid",6],["care",0],["meet",3],["board",2],["plan",6],["cover",0]],"en":"The deal was made in the market on a Saturday, with no paper and no witness. My father would meet the man at the board by the gate, shake hands, and then act as if nothing had happened. He had to bid low at first, because he did not care to look eager. His plan was always the same: wait until the other man was tired, then cover the last offer and walk away. I once asked him for the address of the buyer, and he said he had never needed one.","zh":"这桩买卖是星期六在集市上谈成的，没有纸，也没有证人。我爸会在门边那块木板旁跟人碰头，握个手，然后装作什么都没发生。开头他得压低价，因为他不乐意显出着急的样子。他那套打算从来不变：等对方累了，再把最后那个价码补上，然后走人。有一回我问他买主的地址，他说他从来用不着。"},"dig":{"tw":[["labour",0],["drive",3],["touch",2],["hole",6],["grasp",0],["figure",3],["understand",2],["mud",6],["excavate",0]],"en":"We had to dig a hole for the new tree, and the ground was hard as stone. My grandfather did the labour himself, though he could hardly grasp the handle by the end. He would drive the spade down with his foot, touch the mud at the bottom to see how wet it was, and then go on. He said I should figure out where the roots would go before I started. It took me years to understand what he meant. When they came to excavate the old bed years later, the tree was still standing.","zh":"我们得给新树挖个坑，那土硬得像石头。活是我爷爷自己干的，到后来他几乎握不住锹把。他用脚把铲子蹬下去，摸摸坑底的泥看湿不湿，然后接着挖。他说动手之前我该先琢磨清楚根会往哪儿伸。等我明白他的意思，已经过去好几年了。多年后有人来挖那口旧花坛时，那棵树还站着。"},"dirty":{"tw":[["soil",0],["pollute",3],["change",2],["clean",1],["stuff",6],["foul",3],["splash",3],["trash",6],["grime",0]],"en":"The dog came in dirty from the yard, and there was grime on every step he crossed. He had rolled in something foul and then splashed through the puddle by the gate. My father had to change the cloth on the floor and take the whole thing out to the trash. He said the soil near the road had been polluted for years, and that nothing but weeds would grow there. Do not let him bring that stuff inside, my mother said. I had to give him a bath before he could come in. He was a different animal once he was clean, and he knew it.","zh":"狗从院子里进来，脏得不行，它踏过的每一级台阶上都留下污印。它先在一摊臭东西上滚过，又从门边的水坑里扑腾过来。我爸只好换掉地上的布，把脏东西全都扔到垃圾堆去。他说路边那块土被污染好些年了，除了野草什么都长不出来。我妈说：别让它把那些玩意儿带进屋。我只好先给它洗个澡才让它进来。干净以后它就成了另一只狗，它自己也知道。"},"discover":{"tw":[["break",0],["blow",3],["tell",2],["how",6],["find",2],["see",3],["spy",2],["locate",6],["hear",0]],"en":"I had to discover where the noise was coming from, and I did not know how to start. I could hear it in every room but could not locate it. Then the wind gave a great blow and the door began to break loose in its frame. I went out to see what it was, and I had to tell my mother at once. There was a small pipe under the step, and when I put my hand on it I could find the leak. My neighbour had once worked as a spy, and he said he would have taken half an hour to do the same.","zh":"我得弄清楚这声音是从哪儿来的，可我不知道该从哪儿下手。每个屋里都听得见，就是找不着它在哪。后来一阵大风刮过，那扇门在框子里松开了。我出去看是怎么回事，得马上告诉我妈。台阶底下有根细管子，我手一放上去就摸到了漏的地方。我邻居从前干过谍报，他说同样的事他得花半小时。"},"dog":{"tw":[["tail",0],["tree",3],["catch",2],["cat",6],["track",0],["quest",3],["support",2],["horse",6],["chase",0]],"en":"The old dog could not chase anything now, but he still liked to follow a track along the field. He would put his nose down at the tree by the gate and go on for an hour. Once he caught a cat in the yard and never heard the end of it. He had been a support to my father in the years when there was little else. My grandfather kept a horse in those days, and the two animals were a strange pair, with the dog wagging his tail at the stable door. His last quest was for a bone he had buried himself.","zh":"那条老狗现在什么也追不上了，可它还是喜欢顺着田边跟一条踪迹走。它会在大门旁那棵树底下把鼻子贴到地上，一跟就是一个钟头。有一回它在院子里逮住了一只猫，从此这事被念叨个没完。在那些什么都没有的年头，它是我爸的一个依靠。我爷爷那时候养着一匹马，这两只牲口是奇怪的一对儿，狗总在棚门口摇着尾巴。它最后一次找东西，是找自己埋起来的一根骨头。"}}});
